    <node id="IEEE Transactions on Magnetics">
      <data key="d0">IEEE Transactions on Magnetics</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The `IEEE Transactions on Magnetics` is a specific academic and scientific journal published by the `IEEE`. It is dedicated to publishing papers related to magnetics, covering a broad range of topics within this field.

This journal has published several notable works, including "Multi-objective topology optimization of rotating machines using deep learning" (2019) and "Automated design of magnetic devices by optimizing material distribution" (1996). Other contributions include "An improved magnetic equivalent circuit model for iron-core linear permanent-magnet synchronous motors" and "Surrogate-based MOEA/D for electric motor design with scarce function evaluations." Additionally, it featured a paper on electromagnetic field analysis of electric machines (volume 42, issue 10, pages 3392–3394) and another on the homogenization design method (volume 36, issue 3, pages 574–580). "Topology optimization of nonlinear magnetostatics" was also published in this journal in 2002. The publication is frequently cited in bibliographies as a source for research in magnetics.</data>
