    <node id="Network Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Network Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The architectural design of a neural network, specifically an RNN with attention mechanism and prediction from time-distributed feedforward layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The structure of the network which takes in state representation and outputs probability distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Architecture refers to the design and configuration of the Deep Learning model, including its layers and parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Architecture refers to the design of a neural network, specifically illustrated in Figure 3.8 for efficiency sequence prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Network Architecture is a flowchart illustrating the structure of an end-to-end deep learning model designed for predicting efficiency maps.&lt;SEP&gt;Network Architecture describes the simplified architectural diagram of a neural network for an Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C) algorithm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0dd4b73a53d12770e110415d865cc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640da4d848d6502c665bfc0ea66dce13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a177157c3402545cf649cdb67022050a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fac0a146871deda05d5134b0c361666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5dae035c707962e5992f8ffb5b5c0c7</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288792</data>
    </node>
