    <node id="Internal Knowledge Transfer">
      <data key="d0">Internal Knowledge Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A transfer learning task involving knowledge transfer between IPM motors (IPM to IPM).&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Knowledge Transfer is a specific type of knowledge transfer discussed within the results of Transfer Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Knowledge Transfer is a specific application of transfer learning mentioned requiring 60-65% of the data.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Knowledge Transfer is a scenario where the source and target domains remain the same (Ds = Dt), but the label space changes (Ls ≠ Lt), such as transferring from efficiency map prediction to power factor map.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of knowledge transfer where the domain remains the same ($D_s = D_t$), such as transferring from efficiency maps to power factor maps using the same geometric variations.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Knowledge Transfer is a transfer learning task involving knowledge transfer from an IPM to an IPM, depicted by a red arrow from a "Pre-trained Neural Network" to a "Modified Neural Network".&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of knowledge transfer in neural networks where changes are often concentrated near output layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a73228cc9dfee94628a2eb077e2a4a4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5072e2b75e9621e87c85e7af0ee60311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-193c3a719cf23865bd32e0d110afb409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f237e58ddc202b94dc8ea5b3ef7e3145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fac0a146871deda05d5134b0c361666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ac5f9702a1eb6fb3fd66eadf964396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3e48fade88c3732bf1ffbbe240bea3</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="External Knowledge Transfer">
      <data key="d0">External Knowledge Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A transfer learning task involving knowledge transfer from IPM motors to PM motors (IPM to PM).&lt;SEP&gt;External Knowledge Transfer is a specific type of knowledge transfer discussed within the results of Transfer Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;External Knowledge Transfer is a task involving the transfer of knowledge where both the domain and label parts differ from the original task.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of knowledge transfer.&lt;SEP&gt;External Knowledge Transfer is a scenario involving the prediction of efficiency maps over a different design space (e.g., FSCW Surface-Mounted PM Motor), where domains nor labels necessarily overlap (Ds ≠ Dt and Ls ≠ Lt).&lt;SEP&gt;External Knowledge Transfer is a transfer learning task involving knowledge transfer from an IPM to a PM, depicted by a red arrow from a "Pre-trained Neural Network" to a "Modified Neural Network".&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of knowledge transfer in neural networks where changes are often more evenly distributed across layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a73228cc9dfee94628a2eb077e2a4a4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5072e2b75e9621e87c85e7af0ee60311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-193c3a719cf23865bd32e0d110afb409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f237e58ddc202b94dc8ea5b3ef7e3145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fac0a146871deda05d5134b0c361666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ac5f9702a1eb6fb3fd66eadf964396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3e48fade88c3732bf1ffbbe240bea3</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288830</data>
    </node>
