    <node id="Optimal Solution 3x3 Controller (SeqTO-v_) with TD-Learning">
      <data key="d0">Optimal Solution 3x3 Controller (SeqTO-v_) with TD-Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The optimal solution for a 3x3 controller achieved using SeqTO-v_ and TD-learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2fac0a146871deda05d5134b0c361666</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supervised Learning Task">
      <data key="d0">Supervised Learning Task</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The supervised learning task is set up by describing the data collection process and aims to estimate performance maps.&lt;SEP&gt;A Supervised Learning Task is the framework within which the reinforcement learning problem is set up for analysis, particularly for value estimation.&lt;SEP&gt;The value estimation problem can be framed as a supervised learning task where a neural network's Q(s, a) predicts the Q_π(S, A) as a 'true' label.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a600bc388389f7228161e154b865877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f74efd7c2930be98c8e7ee58bb7f2201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288951</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bayesian Learning Approach">
      <data key="d0">Bayesian Learning Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A Bayesian learning approach is used to address the issue of uncertainty in trained networks within the cold start supervised learning task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Map Estimation">
      <data key="d0">Performance Map Estimation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance map estimation marks the conclusion of the cold start supervised learning task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transfer Learning Strategy">
      <data key="d0">Transfer Learning Strategy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A transfer learning strategy is discussed for extending trained networks to predict performance maps for new geometries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Efficiency Map Calculation Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Efficiency Map Calculation Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">This procedure is detailed in Figure 3.5 and is based on the work of Mohammadi and Lowther (2017) to calculate efficiency maps.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure for calculating motor efficiency maps, which includes defining drive and excitation conditions in Stage 1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28be27ccbb95fc691bf7d1ab7fac43a1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288890</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mohammadi and Lowther 2017">
      <data key="d0">Mohammadi and Lowther 2017</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A publication referenced for the reduced prediction time of performance maps compared to traditional approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;This is a reference indicating the source for the current efficiency map calculation procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Mohammadi and Lowther 2017 refers to a publication describing a procedure for calculating performance maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b36856e6868820792611d3fddfdfc66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Simcenter MotorSolve">
      <data key="d0">Simcenter MotorSolve</data>
      <data key="d1">software</data>
      <data key="d2">Simcenter MotorSolve is a software used for electromagnetic FE simulations to obtain dq flux linkages.&lt;SEP&gt;Simcenter MotorSolve is a Finite Element (FE) software used for analyzing motor designs and generating training data for machine learning models.&lt;SEP&gt;Simcenter MotorSolve is a software accessible via http://www.infolytica.com/.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a37e88914ecd388d79917c1c24f82fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285254</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DQ Flux Linkages">
      <data key="d0">DQ Flux Linkages</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">DQ flux linkages are obtained from electromagnetic FE simulations for characterization in Stage 1.&lt;SEP&gt;DQ Flux Linkages are the predicted output of the neural network model, representing a specific electrical parameter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17fa5f6a446284811fca7ceb6337e9ab</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288869</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flux Linkage Maps">
      <data key="d0">Flux Linkage Maps</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Maps constructed from dq flux linkages using 2nd-degree polynomials as functions of dq currents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285254</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DQ Currents">
      <data key="d0">DQ Currents</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">DQ currents are used as input for FE simulations to obtain dq flux linkages and for constructing flux linkage maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Maximum-Torque-Per-Ampere">
      <data key="d0">Maximum-Torque-Per-Ampere</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">This is a control strategy used in Stage 2 to find optimal excitation conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flux Weakening">
      <data key="d0">Flux Weakening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">This is a control strategy used in Stage 2 to find optimal excitation conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91f06583cd9261910571520c3ff2088e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
