    <node id="A2C Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">A2C Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A2C (Advantage Actor-Critic) is an algorithm, specifically a reinforcement learning algorithm, tested for convergence and performance, and employed to learn from experience and generalize across scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;The A2C algorithm is an optimization algorithm that provides solutions for core designs, including the conventional geometry, and is based on a probabilistic nature.&lt;SEP&gt;The A2C (Actor-Critic) algorithm is a reinforcement learning method that uses a probabilistic policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The A2C algorithm's performance and generalizability are evaluated using the scenarios defined in the table. The term A2C stands for Advantage Actor-Critic.&lt;SEP&gt;The A2C algorithm is a method discussed in the context of topology optimization of the C-core.&lt;SEP&gt;The A2C Algorithm is a specific algorithm mentioned in the surrounding context, implicated in configuring the evolving lime green shape for optimal magnetic core design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68f5932d6d7a0e838c4c7ec90c8f340d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c2c4cc1ff144256a7c660b31a82de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df545da4858de5af7705d69fba2707ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b83022ca44128f92a414d02c9b7fc66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6504e2cf679305513217b8548174a68b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
