    <node id="Tabular QL">
      <data key="d0">Tabular QL</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Tabular QL is a form of Q-Learning where the Q-values are stored in a table, used here with SeqTO-v1.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of Q-learning where states and actions are discrete and stored in a table, discussed in Chapter 4 Section 4.5.3.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of Q-learning discussed in Section 4.5.3 and 4.9.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific type of Q-Learning algorithm, referred to as (SeqTO-v⊥).&lt;SEP&gt;Tabular QL is a method mentioned as having similar state representation results to the Deep Q-Learning approach for the C-core problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a0921c09c7af3fdaeac2a38ff90bbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d519cd75c14207ceeaef0cf84051a1d1</data>
