    <node id="Finite Element Analysis (FEA)">
      <data key="d0">Finite Element Analysis (FEA)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">FEA, specifically MAGNET v2020.2, is used to gather ground truth, labels, and evaluations for statistical learning experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Finite Element Analysis (FEA) is a method within physics-based models that provides accurate analysis of electric machines, and is the method of choice for machine designers.&lt;SEP&gt;FEA is a simulation method used to estimate force and torque, often exhibiting tighter and lower percentage errors compared to MEC, and suitable for final design analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Finite Element Analysis is a numerical method suggested by the meshed grid in Diagram (b) for simulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b83022ca44128f92a414d02c9b7fc66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d146c06d89d470b7db435c475826c0e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
