    <node id="Ground Truth">
      <data key="d0">Ground Truth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ground truth refers to the verified data or information used as a basis for comparison in statistical learning experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground truth refers to the actual, known values against which the model's predictions are compared to calculate error.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground truth refers to the actual, known values against which predictions are compared to determine errors.&lt;SEP&gt;The true, known label or value of data, often not available for comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground truth refers to the reliable and verified data used for comparison and validation of predictions or models.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground truth refers to the factual data or exact information that is known to be true, used as a baseline for comparison with model predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38ad7ba535a3b44f510acc91b0e8d5f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0a01577276faacfde89d458d90e662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf789c1974c43fd1722237522bebd446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb99d0c44b7c6ee269cad3cce40b7be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cc2b02ae3a119d92f0d1a7f6617885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289035</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Labels">
      <data key="d0">Labels</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Labels are classifications or tags associated with data, used for training and evaluating supervised learning models.</data>
