    </node>
    <node id="Electromagnetic Force">
      <data key="d0">Electromagnetic Force</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Electromagnetic force is a performance characteristic of an electric machine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285296</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Torque">
      <data key="d0">Torque</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Torque is a global performance quantity used to evaluate designs in fast prototyping with analytic models, and is proportional to state variables in machine systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Torque is a performance characteristic of an electric machine.&lt;SEP&gt;Torque is an electromagnetic quantity computed using FE simulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Input values to the sequence-based model, represented as Tem*.&lt;SEP&gt;The value of torque is compared with the conventional design of a C-core.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285296</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fields">
      <data key="d0">Fields</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fields refer to magnetic or electric fields, a performance characteristic of an electric machine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285296</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Losses Distribution Maps">
      <data key="d0">Losses Distribution Maps</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Losses distribution maps are performance characteristics of an electric machine, indicating energy loss.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285296</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Optimization Task">
      <data key="d0">Optimization Task</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An optimization task aims to achieve objectives like minimizing torque ripple, increasing average torque, and efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285297</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Torque Ripple">
      <data key="d0">Torque Ripple</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Torque ripple is a global quantity, usually with a single output value, for which surrogates are designed.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance parameter for electric machines, referring to periodic variations in output torque.&lt;SEP&gt;Torque ripple is an undesirable variation in torque, which an optimization task aims to minimize.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285298</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Average Torque">
      <data key="d0">Average Torque</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Average Torque is a critical global performance parameter and key outcome metric for electric machines, particularly the Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM). It represents a measurement of the rotational force produced by the SynRM, and its positive magnitude is often targeted for maximization in optimization tasks.

This metric is used to evaluate the performance of motors and is frequently employed as an objective function in various optimization processes. For instance, an optimization task might aim to increase the average torque, and in specific contexts, achieving a value of '3.40 N-m' is reported as an optimized average torque for the SynRM, notably improved by optimized geometry or through methods like TD-learning with SeqTO-v1. A baseline for average torque in SynRM applications is sometimes set, such as 2.5 N-m, with subsequent optimization efforts aiming to surpass this value. Certain modeling methods can effectively predict this crucial performance indicator.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5a390cc7143789eccd25f5f3623694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7b73719952876f4f9c0e6b4efe0027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b63cf0d438e93eb8fd05fc3ffbbb91e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f519dcf3231dec106e81c35523ed6914&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0011b0a6062b8a1499810eced96d7d94</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288947</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model">
      <data key="d0">Model</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A model is a simplification of reality that can be useful for explaining, predicting, and understanding the universe, even if it is not a perfect representation of phenomena.&lt;SEP&gt;A model is an approximation of reality, used for simplification and idealization.&lt;SEP&gt;The model efficiently approximates field distribution, enabling generation for new geometries at lower computational costs with parallelizability over GPUs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4389bce8e015dd342452266c2e8a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285298</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reality">
      <data key="d0">Reality</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reality is the actual state of things, which a model approximates but does not perfectly reflect.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75365c11d58d9301541e75f2ba5f03ec</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285299</data>
    </node>
