    <node id="Deep Learning">
      <data key="d0">Deep Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep Learning (DL) is a modern machine learning technique and a significant subfield of machine learning. It achieved prominence starting in the 1940s, with its evolution being closely tied to the development of deep networks. Deep learning operates by utilizing artificial neural networks composed of multiple layers to learn data representations with varying levels of abstraction, typically employing a training dataset. This process is often facilitated by high-performance computing.

Deep Learning is applied in various domains, demonstrating its versatility. It is utilized for predicting field distribution in electromagnetic problems and electromagnetic devices, and specifically for magnetic field estimation and efficiency map prediction in motor drives. Furthermore, Deep Learning has been explored in the context of smart grids, topological design, and to accelerate Topology Optimization. Its application in neural networks has also been a subject of extensive research, exemplified by works such as "Deep learning in neural networks: An overview" (2015).&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning is a method used in the process depicted in Figure 2.11, leading to field predictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning is a subset of machine learning that uses neural networks with multiple layers to learn representations of data.&lt;SEP&gt;A subfield of machine learning that uses multi-layered neural networks to learn from data.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Learning (DL) is a concept that combines with Reinforcement Learning to form the Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) paradigm of algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e02179750b3f9b10c33f013ef970dc4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4cb77e8b268b787c61c98919fbdbaff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1e3ef3a96efc33efd9047031ab15a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03395909e238b7701943add27146739b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-294177d434050aa2bd996039510efe9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2e27a9a79daf5a813690efa01766eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-588116b5242516d003d1e70d48a7f42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d320c7db870069aad6b0a37ec04c740b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b78525002f5dfa42398879cc72242c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd6ce2b178e669e439db6c5cb7f00f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-403239ec5550f149ced3802b6c18600b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289186</data>
