    <node id="Additive Manufacturing">
      <data key="d0">Additive Manufacturing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Additive Manufacturing (AM) is a technique whose development has increased the significance of Topology Optimization in the manufacturing industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Additive manufacturing is a field where progress has led to renewed attention for the homogenization method.&lt;SEP&gt;A process of making three-dimensional solid objects from a digital design.&lt;SEP&gt;A manufacturing technique used for customizing automotive structural components.&lt;SEP&gt;Additive Manufacturing is the application area for topology optimization reviewed in the paper "A review of topology optimization for additive manufacturing: Status and challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;A manufacturing process that builds three-dimensional objects by adding material layer by layer, including techniques like selective laser sintering (SLS) or direct metal laser sintering (DMLS).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e02179750b3f9b10c33f013ef970dc4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2e27a9a79daf5a813690efa01766eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c232c16db2cb946ab34105a48ebff79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-588116b5242516d003d1e70d48a7f42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
