    <node id="Random Search">
      <data key="d0">Random Search</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Random search is a common method used to find optimal values for hyperparameters in machine learning models.&lt;SEP&gt;Random search is a common method for arriving at optimal values of hyperparameters during model selection.&lt;SEP&gt;A computationally cheaper method for hyperparameter optimization, used to find an optimal configuration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ad7ba535a3b44f510acc91b0e8d5f1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285314</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grid Search">
      <data key="d0">Grid Search</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Grid search is a common method used to find optimal values for hyperparameters in machine learning models.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid search is a common method for arriving at optimal values of hyperparameters during model selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid search is an exhaustive searching through a manually specified subset of the hyperparameter space of a learning algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid Search is a method performed to determine the percentage of data required for transfer learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f237e58ddc202b94dc8ea5b3ef7e3145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ad7ba535a3b44f510acc91b0e8d5f1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geron 2019">
      <data key="d0">Geron 2019</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Geron 2019 refers to a publication that discusses random search and grid search for hyperparameter optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;This refers to a publication cited for information on batch-normalization layers and hyperparameters optimization methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Geron 2019 is a reference cited for the concept of a confusion matrix.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ad7ba535a3b44f510acc91b0e8d5f1</data>
