    <node id="3x3 Controller">
      <data key="d0">3x3 Controller</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The 3x3 controller is a type of control mechanism utilized in optimization tasks, particularly mentioned in the context of SeqTO-vl and TD-learning for a C-core design. This controller type has been used with both tabular and function approximator forms of Q-Learning, and it is also employed in conjunction with Deep Q-Learning to fill linear iron material for the C-core design.

Characterized by a coarser granularity compared to the 1x1 controller, the 3x3 controller has demonstrated a generated force of 51 N in certain applications. However, it has been identified as a previous limitation for generating complex structures due to its restricted action capabilities. The 3x3 controller serves as a point of comparison for the 1x1 controller and has been noted to perform less optimally than the 1x1 controller for electrical steel. It is understood as a component or system that is optimized using the SeqTO-vl method with TD-learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e0691c9f7251ff59c05b1bc277ea93e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6719c866b8100236897a8ad6ae78d11f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526ac278068ab9cbf72c11fd3817672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7e662d13f8f799c0011dbabf78f253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33feda9b614873c4d42a0aa2ba3f7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a0921c09c7af3fdaeac2a38ff90bbb</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288758</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TD-Learning">
      <data key="d0">TD-Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">TD-Learning, or Temporal Difference learning, is a reinforcement learning (RL) algorithm primarily used for optimization tasks. It is a model-free method that distinguishes itself from Monte Carlo methods by employing bootstrapping: instead of waiting for the full sum of rewards, it updates value estimates based on other learned estimates, particularly an estimate of future returns. This allows TD-Learning to learn incrementally throughout an episode, even from incomplete episodes, and to update value estimates based on the agent's generated experience in the form of (state, action, next_state, reward) tuples.

Within the context of topology optimization, TD-Learning has been explored as a tree search-based heuristic algorithm, specifically within the SeqTO environment and in conjunction with SeqTO-v1 for sequence-based topology optimization. It has been applied to SynRM (Synchronous Reluctance Machine) optimization, where it has shown similar improvements to Genetic Algorithms (GA) in terms of torque optimization. TD-Learning has also been utilized for C-core results, based on specific design setups, and is mentioned as a method for policy evaluation and for a control system. A specific form of the TD-learning update rule is seen in Q-learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19e84f4051b2d1d639403e518dc4ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e759e174fdc4ef458e871149c5bf316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1474f4155ebb5657d8ca7f3c0d29b49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526ac278068ab9cbf72c11fd3817672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b63cf0d438e93eb8fd05fc3ffbbb91e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28d95920dc2d89112c02d6c86f6d7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56c95146eb3d0e8591ffefd6ab679ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146167a8b3388ece49f9a67ad320dd0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f519dcf3231dec106e81c35523ed6914&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33feda9b614873c4d42a0aa2ba3f7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c8e2c74dbd2fe78b4f64f43cd17e839</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288760</data>
