    <node id="Synchronous Reluctance Motors">
      <data key="d0">Synchronous Reluctance Motors</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of electric motor for which conventional rotor designs are discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of electric motor that uses reluctance torque for its operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous reluctance motors are electric motors that utilize reluctance torque for operation, with their rotor designs featuring specific lamination techniques to create magnetic barriers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-588116b5242516d003d1e70d48a7f42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d562d92283cc555ded41962ea3fb9e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
