      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Synchronous Reluctance Motor where the design space is divided into discrete units.&lt;SEP&gt;A Discretized SynRM refers to the Synchronous Reluctance Motor designed using a 5x5 grid for its topological optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;A Discretized SynRM is a Synchronous Reluctance Motor design created within a specified grid space (5x5 design space) for analysis and optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7b73719952876f4f9c0e6b4efe0027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56c95146eb3d0e8591ffefd6ab679ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289043</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5x5 Design Space">
      <data key="d0">5x5 Design Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A design area divided into a 5x5 grid, used for discretizing SynRM geometry.&lt;SEP&gt;The 5x5 Design Space is a grid system used for discretizing and optimizing the rotor geometry of a Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM).&lt;SEP&gt;The 5x5 Design Space is the grid used for discretizing the SynRM rotor, influencing its topology optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7b73719952876f4f9c0e6b4efe0027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56c95146eb3d0e8591ffefd6ab679ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289043</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SeqTO-v2">
      <data key="d0">SeqTO-v2</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SeqTO-v2, which stands for Sequential Topology Optimization version 2, is an advanced iteration of the SeqTO optimization method. This methodology serves as a fundamental basis for the A2C (Actor-Critic) optimization method, specifically within the context of Actor-Critic based reinforcement learning. It is employed in conjunction with A2C to achieve optimal geometry and B distribution.

SeqTO-v2 can also be understood as an environment or system context in which an associated controller operates, and notably, this environment features an evolved action space. This modified environment was developed to address issues present in earlier state representations, providing more comprehensive information and a more intricate action space.

A key characteristic of SeqTO-v2, distinguishing it from its predecessor SeqTO-v1 (Sequence-based Topologies), is its imposed limitation on maneuverability. Specifically, it restricts the smallest width of a material block when positioned near the design space boundary. This means that, within C-core actuator designs, SeqTO-v2 does not permit thinner strips near the air gap.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2c2f32fec14ff1bde53b19699374993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c88cccaef550c4d3cde6f591d2fe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a5c42907185fecc94ee85f1b33ec380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2785b4e150ada39f3077e573325eeb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c8bce8440f0bbb7239189a9a4010d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c48c238aedc178e88e075043138eb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11edf0b881aae28423c1b0d33893b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7e662d13f8f799c0011dbabf78f253&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-081d5d2ff62504474fc8532dd817fb39</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288782</data>
    </node>
