    <node id="RL">
      <data key="d0">RL</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Reinforcement Learning, a type of machine learning concerned with how intelligent agents ought to take actions in an environment to maximize the notion of cumulative reward.&lt;SEP&gt;RL, or Reinforcement Learning, is an area of machine learning concerned with how software agents ought to take actions in an environment to maximize some notion of cumulative reward.&lt;SEP&gt;RL (Reinforcement Learning) is an optimization method used with SeqTO (Sequential Topology Optimization) for C-core actuator design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c8bce8440f0bbb7239189a9a4010d7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DL">
      <data key="d0">DL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep Learning, a subfield of machine learning inspired by the structure and function of the brain.&lt;SEP&gt;DL, or Deep Learning, is a subfield of machine learning involving deep neural networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
