    <node id="Q-Network">
      <data key="d0">Q-Network</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A neural network structure used to approximate Q-values in Q-learning.&lt;SEP&gt;A neural network specifically referred to as DQN, trained to find an optimal policy greedy on the cumulated reward function within the Deep Q-learning algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-network is a neural network that provides an estimate for the action-value function, denoted by $\\hat{Q}(S_t, A_t, w)$.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-Network is neural network used in Q-learning to estimate action-values, which is updated based on the squared error gradient.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-Network is a component within a reinforcement learning context, illustrated with two different setup approaches in the image.&lt;SEP&gt;The Q-network is a neural network that approximates the Q-function, used to estimate action-values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-023a66b0b7b2235f3cc11df422f013f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24ed737fb6aa8500ccd706bf246c499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35bf46c88c50e423b73a91a41f7f95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7d0fc487b66b91a1d8bae6610798e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47</data>
