    <node id="A2C">
      <data key="d0">A2C</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A2C, which stands for Advantage Actor-Critic, is a reinforcement learning (RL) algorithm. It is an advanced form of the Actor-Critic model and is characterized by its use of a stochastic policy, where it samples all actions based on probability, unlike Q-Learning's often deterministic or greedy selection. A2C is employed for gradient calculation within the reinforcement learning framework.

Furthermore, A2C is described as an optimization algorithm, particularly when based on SeqTO-v2. In this context, it has been used as an RL-based agent for excitation scenarios, specifically for generating optimal geometry and determining magnetic flux density (B) distribution. One application mentioned is its use in determining optimal C-core geometry, which has resulted in a force of 85.7 N and involved 125,000 Finite Element (FE) Calls. Beyond geometry, A2C agents are utilized to obtain magnetic flux density distribution and identify optimal design solutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7133594b2e19b403575b42aef1cafffb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e0300f86edc3c358dfc2a9374e88a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2c2f32fec14ff1bde53b19699374993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a5c42907185fecc94ee85f1b33ec380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5072e2b75e9621e87c85e7af0ee60311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2785b4e150ada39f3077e573325eeb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b6b9bf681c07677d8af5a26068c52f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11edf0b881aae28423c1b0d33893b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5dae035c707962e5992f8ffb5b5c0c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-081d5d2ff62504474fc8532dd817fb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288791</data>
    </node>
