    <node id="Physics-Informed Deep Learning">
      <data key="d0">Physics-Informed Deep Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Physics-Informed Deep Learning methods can be used for EM analysis by directly solving governing partial differential equations (PDEs).&lt;SEP&gt;Physics-informed deep learning is a method used to solve PDEs by incorporating physical laws into the loss function of a neural network.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governing Partial Differential Equations">
      <data key="d0">Governing Partial Differential Equations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Governing Partial Differential Equations (PDEs) describe physical laws and can be solved using physics-informed deep learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Optimal Solution">
      <data key="d0">Optimal Solution</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The ideal outcome or design that faster learning aims to converge towards through methods like generalizability.&lt;SEP&gt;The optimal solution refers to the best possible design or configuration for an electromagnetic device.&lt;SEP&gt;The optimal solution represents the best possible configuration or outcome achieved by a system, in this context, for a 3x3 controller within a C-core design domain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9360ea49ebcfafb62140f053dfc1f70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33feda9b614873c4d42a0aa2ba3f7c8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Reinforcement Learning Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Deep Reinforcement Learning Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep Reinforcement Learning Algorithms are used for sequence-based topology optimization and sequential decision making.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Reinforcement Learning Algorithms are many algorithms that use this type of weight update, especially those based on SARSA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f59209c2113faa8129ee1fd7aa6b8e</data>
