    <node id="Partial Differential Equations">
      <data key="d0">Partial Differential Equations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Partial Differential Equations (PDEs) are governing equations that physics-informed deep learning methods aim to solve.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial Differential Equations (PDEs) are mathematical equations that can be solved using physics-informed deep learning methods for EM analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f5af4d3dcb1894cb22db778a1e1b744</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285392</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A global optimization method applied in the electromagnetic field, based on mutation and cross-over.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic algorithms are a global optimization method applied in electromagnetic fields that eliminate inferior solutions and advance superior solutions through mutation and cross-over.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic Algorithms (GAs) are a specific type of Evolutionary Algorithm mentioned in the surrounding text.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic Algorithms (GA) are an artificial intelligence method used in conjunction with Topology Optimization for design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c8eeb9e91e5bd71f6909085d5d4a52e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad46225ae0d5f3835a9bda1ed8158d48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75b68f2c0143d85fc982bac91ab7a190</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289096</data>
    </node>
