    <node id="MC Sampling">
      <data key="d0">MC Sampling</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method that improved accuracy (normalized mean squared error) by around 10% and is used to compute uncertainty maps.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique where multiple samples are taken to approximate an integral or distribution, used for uncertainty quantification and improved accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da0a01577276faacfde89d458d90e662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4389bce8e015dd342452266c2e8a65</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accuracy">
      <data key="d0">Accuracy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric, specifically normalized mean squared error, that improved by 10% due to MC sampling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d4389bce8e015dd342452266c2e8a65</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285431</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computational Costs">
      <data key="d0">Computational Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The costs associated with computation that are lowered by the model's efficient approximation of field distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;Computational Costs refer to the expenses or resources associated with using advanced tools and modeling in the design cycle, a key focus for improvement in the thesis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d4389bce8e015dd342452266c2e8a65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0af18e12848c44ab0d9b01471789474</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288734</data>
    </node>
