    <node id="Ghorbanian, Salimi, and Lowther (2017)">
      <data key="d0">Ghorbanian, Salimi, and Lowther (2017)</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Researchers cited for specifying product requirements in the Design Phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Ghorbanian, Salimi, and Lowther (2017) are researchers cited for their contributions to the development of alternative surrogate models.&lt;SEP&gt;Authors credited for work on model capacity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dot Product">
      <data key="d0">Dot Product</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The dot product is a mathematical operation computed by both FC and CONV layers between their weights and activations, followed by a non-linear activation function.&lt;SEP&gt;The dot product is a mathematical operation used to combine two vectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Linear Activation Function">
      <data key="d0">Non-Linear Activation Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A non-linear activation function is applied after the dot product computation in FC and CONV layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ReLU">
      <data key="d0">ReLU</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit) is an activation function used within the convolutional layers of the DL model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Goodfellow, Bengio, and Courville 2016">
      <data key="d0">Goodfellow, Bengio, and Courville 2016</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to a publication that provides information on ReLU and max-pooling, contributing to the DL model's architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Goodfellow, Bengio, and Courville 2016 is a reference cited for the softmax approach of policy parametrization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e3e1dd6f2a21d7997b5fa281b76b709</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
