    <node id="Kernel Size">
      <data key="d0">Kernel Size</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Kernel size is a hyperparameter influencing model capacity and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Kernel size refers to the dimensions of the convolutional filter.&lt;SEP&gt;Kernel size is a parameter in neural networks, and its impact on capturing spatially far relations is discussed in the context of dilation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a4b902f2347e5fea9d43e606ce167ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8854ea1ca7b618b176856798664355f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288776</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Number of Kernels">
      <data key="d0">Number of Kernels</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The number of kernels (or filters) is a hyperparameter influencing model capacity and performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regularization Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Regularization Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Regularization parameters are settings that help ensure the model has sufficient capacity to capture problem complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285455</data>
    </node>
