      <data key="d0">Figure 2.7</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Figure 2.7 illustrates the set of learnable filters/kernels in a convolutional layer and the dense kernel used for grouping pixels.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2.7 is another figure referenced in the text that shows a dense kernel, contrasting with Figure 2.9.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a4b902f2347e5fea9d43e606ce167ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289016</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Figure 2.11">
      <data key="d0">Figure 2.11</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Figure 2.11, along with Figure 2.8, shows the DL model architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2.11 refers to an external figure mentioned on page 42 that, along with Figure 2.8, shows the Deep Learning model.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2.11 is a multi-part figure displaying the process from CAD modeling to deep learning and FEA results for magnetic field predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8b78525002f5dfa42398879cc72242c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a177157c3402545cf649cdb67022050a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f3b0d30beebae149e306398e8c2b1b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289001</data>
