    <node id="Data Collection Bias">
      <data key="d0">Data Collection Bias</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data collection bias is an issue that can be introduced to a model if the training samples are biased, affecting the generalizability of a surrogate Deep Learning model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d519cd75c14207ceeaef0cf84051a1d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285458</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unseen New Geometry">
      <data key="d0">Unseen New Geometry</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An unseen new geometry refers to a design space part not covered by the training data, leading to unreliable performance of ML models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d519cd75c14207ceeaef0cf84051a1d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285458</data>
    </node>
