    <node id="Material (Volume) Constraint">
      <data key="d0">Material (Volume) Constraint</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The material (volume) constraint is a condition in supervised learning that is treated as a target to match rather than a true inequality constraint due to the nature of loss function minimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d519cd75c14207ceeaef0cf84051a1d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Loss Function">
      <data key="d0">Loss Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Loss Function is a mathematical function that quantifies the error between predicted and actual values, serving as a critical component in machine learning and optimization problems. It measures the quality of a set of parameters by assessing their agreement with ground truth targets in training data. This function is instrumental in optimization algorithms, where its primary goal is to minimize the error.

Derived theoretically from equations like the Mean Squared Error (MSE), a loss function drives the learning process, particularly in value-based Reinforcement Learning (RL) methods, through its minimization. The gradient of the loss function can be determined to calculate the error on an experience trajectory, aiding in model improvement. When a loss function is non-differentiable, Evolutionary Algorithms can be particularly effective for optimization. Its entire expression often serves as the loss function for training neural networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9360ea49ebcfafb62140f053dfc1f70c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad46225ae0d5f3835a9bda1ed8158d48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03395909e238b7701943add27146739b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f74efd7c2930be98c8e7ee58bb7f2201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023a66b0b7b2235f3cc11df422f013f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24ed737fb6aa8500ccd706bf246c499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d519cd75c14207ceeaef0cf84051a1d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289099</data>
    </node>
