      <data key="d0">Mou et al. (2016)</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Mou et al. (2016) is a reference cited in the context of transfer learning, regarding a predictor starting its learning from extracted knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285480</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pre-Trained Network">
      <data key="d0">Pre-Trained Network</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A pre-trained network is a neural network that has already learned knowledge from a related task and can be adapted for new tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A network portion identified as prior knowledge, useful for new tasks and representing common knowledge between source and target tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a73228cc9dfee94628a2eb077e2a4a4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285480</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Motor Configurations">
      <data key="d0">Motor Configurations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Motor configurations refer to the various designs of motors, for which generating massive datasets individually would be impossible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285480</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Power Factor">
      <data key="d0">Power Factor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A performance parameter of an electric motor drive.&lt;SEP&gt;Power factor is a performance metric for motor drives, which can be predicted by surrogate models.&lt;SEP&gt;Power Factor is a key metric calculated for electric motors and is part of the performance maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7fda188f6e0be572dc98e8f2a6ca4e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36856e6868820792611d3fddfdfc66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289416</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Loss Maps">
      <data key="d0">Loss Maps</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Loss maps show the energy losses in a motor, and surrogates can be created for their prediction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electric Motor Drives">
      <data key="d0">Electric Motor Drives</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Other architectures and methodologies are explored for predicting performance maps of these devices.&lt;SEP&gt;The electric motor drives are the subject of an automated design and manufacturing process.&lt;SEP&gt;Devices for which performance parameters are predicted using deep networks like CNNs and RNNs.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric motor drives are systems that use electric motors, to which deep neural networks are applied for performance prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric motor drives are the subject of the V-Design and Manufacturing Cycle, indicating a product development focus for this technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a90b78ebd0801e79ae02815c13eb5b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36856e6868820792611d3fddfdfc66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0af18e12848c44ab0d9b01471789474</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288729</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Synchronous AC Machines">
      <data key="d0">Synchronous AC Machines</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Synchronous AC machines are a type of electric motor, including IPM and FSCW PM types, studied in the context of transfer learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous AC Machines are a type of electric motor, including interior permanent magnet (IPM) and fractional-slot concentrated winding permanent magnet (FSCW PM) machines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f6cebd0187b0c1924a3e6491e8ebe8</data>
