    <node id="Final Element Simulation">
      <data key="d0">Final Element Simulation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Final Element (FE) simulation is a conventional method used to obtain ground truth results against which neural network predictions can be compared.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285486</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Neural Network">
      <data key="d0">Deep Neural Network</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep neural network is trained in a supervised manner to map magnetic field distribution for various geometric complexities.&lt;SEP&gt;A deep neural network is a computational model trained to predict performance maps for different motor training topologies.&lt;SEP&gt;A deep neural network (DNN) is a type of neural network that can act as a surrogate to FE simulations, but requires significant computational resources for training data generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb0bf44fcf7466c35982fd3bb8ae7ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a90b78ebd0801e79ae02815c13eb5b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
