      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A publication where the use of deep networks for predicting performance parameters of electric motor drives is extended.&lt;SEP&gt;Khan et al. 2020a is a reference (paper or book) where labels were efficiency values for each design point.&lt;SEP&gt;Khan et al. 2020a refers to a publication related to a procedure for calculating performance maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b36856e6868820792611d3fddfdfc66f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3e48fade88c3732bf1ffbbe240bea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285489</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Optimal Electromagnetic Quantities">
      <data key="d0">Optimal Electromagnetic Quantities</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Optimal electromagnetic quantities include torque, efficiency, and power factor, computed using FE simulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285489</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model-Based Knowledge Transfer">
      <data key="d0">Model-Based Knowledge Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Model-based knowledge transfer is a methodology in transfer learning, focusing on transferring knowledge through pre-trained models.&lt;SEP&gt;Model-based knowledge transfer is the most popular methodology for DNNs in the field of machine learning, focusing on enhancing generalizability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5d3e48fade88c3732bf1ffbbe240bea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679159f51a7b3c245fdff9193fd1ef89</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285489</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Statistical Learning Methodologies">
      <data key="d0">Statistical Learning Methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Modern statistical learning methodologies are employed in the field, with generalizability being a key aspect for all techniques.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285489</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Partial Differential Equations (PDEs)">
      <data key="d0">Partial Differential Equations (PDEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PDEs are governing equations that can be solved using physics-informed deep learning methods in EM analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Collection">
      <data key="d0">Data Collection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of gathering data for training models, including data from coils, transformers, and IPM motors.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Collection is a method that involves gathering data for analysis, specifically mentioned in the context of Prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of gathering data for training deep learning networks and for finite element-based performance evaluation in reinforcement learning, noted as computationally expensive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb0bf44fcf7466c35982fd3bb8ae7ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5072e2b75e9621e87c85e7af0ee60311</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Learning (DL) Networks">
      <data key="d0">Deep Learning (DL) Networks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep Learning networks are a type of neural network that require data for training and are used in various machine learning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Finite Element (FE)-Based Performance Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Finite Element (FE)-Based Performance Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method used for evaluating the performance of Reinforcement Learning agents, which can be computationally expensive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285490</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reinforcement Learning (RL) Agents">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning (RL) Agents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RL agents are intelligent systems that learn to make decisions by interacting with an environment, and their performance can be evaluated using FE-based methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supervised Learning Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Supervised Learning Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of machine learning task where a model learns from labeled training data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Knowledge Transfer">
      <data key="d0">Knowledge Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of applying knowledge gained from one task to another.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge Transfer refers to the timely transfer of weights from the Behaviour Policy to the Target Policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge Transfer is a concept explored in Chapter 3 for Supervised Learning tasks, aiming to reduce the simulation data needed for training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a73228cc9dfee94628a2eb077e2a4a4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Task DL Network">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Task DL Network</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of Deep Learning network capable of accumulating knowledge across multiple tasks, potentially reducing the need for simulation data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multiple Independent Agents">
      <data key="d0">Multiple Independent Agents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">These are agents in RL-based problems that can interact with different instances of the environment in parallel to explore state-action space efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Physics/Multiobjective TO Problem">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Physics/Multiobjective TO Problem</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A complex Topology Optimization problem involving multiple physical phenomena and multiple objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SeqTO- $v { \boldsymbol { \mathcal { Z } } }$">
      <data key="d0">SeqTO- $v { \boldsymbol { \mathcal { Z } } }$</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SeqTO- $v { \boldsymbol { \mathcal { Z } } }$ is a method that increased generalizability and reduced computational burden compared to SeqTO- $v l$, but has limitations in structural granularity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SeqTO- $v l$">
      <data key="d0">SeqTO- $v l$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An unspecified method or system with higher computation burden and lower generalizability compared to SeqTO- $v { \boldsymbol { \mathcal { Z } } }$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep RL Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Deep RL Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep Reinforcement Learning algorithms are a class of algorithms that combine deep neural networks with reinforcement learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)">
      <data key="d0">Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">PPO is a Deep RL algorithm known for being comparatively faster and more robust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Soft Actor-Critic (SAC)">
      <data key="d0">Soft Actor-Critic (SAC)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SAC is a Deep RL algorithm known for being comparatively faster and more robust.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Curiosity-Based Learning">
      <data key="d0">Curiosity-Based Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Curiosity-based learning is a learning methodology that is comparatively faster and more robust than other Deep RL algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a93df544481c46867db2b00e4b597341</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285493</data>
