    <node id="Q-Table">
      <data key="d0">Q-Table</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A Q-table stores action-value functions in Q-Learning, with examples found in Tables 4.3 and 5.2.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-table is a matrix-like data structure that represents Q-values, which are action-value function values for taking specific actions in given states within Q-Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-Table is a data structure used in reinforcement learning to store the learned action-values for each state-action pair. The weight vector $w$ can be a flattened representation of a Q-Table.&lt;SEP&gt;A Q-table is a tabular representation used in Q-learning to store Q-values, which represent the estimated utility of taking a particular action from a given state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ceb1ac6e54fec53c601d8b38f2b338d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c2a865bc92e157d3426a926d7ddd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca0b752852f034cec7766c7e6e92af67</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288972</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C-Core Results">
      <data key="d0">C-Core Results</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">These are results obtained from the Genetic Algorithm using the SeqTO-v1 environment for a C-core, including armature force comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;C-core results refer to the outcomes obtained from the Genetic Algorithm using the SeqTO-v1 environment, specifically regarding armature force.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af2139266a69c7c4fede66d615ca0684</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289413</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Midha et al. (2019)">
      <data key="d0">Midha et al. (2019)</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Midha et al. refers to researchers responsible for a filtering technique used in GA optimization results.&lt;SEP&gt;Authors of a work published in 2019 that introduced GA+ filters and whose previous results are used for performance improvement comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Midha et al. (2019) refers to researchers who conducted previous work on topology optimization, providing comparative data for armature force using an ON/OFF based Topology Optimization algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Midha et al. (2019) refers to a work that developed the GA+filters method for optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0a87e071d0b56bc121b18a65c5875d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af2139266a69c7c4fede66d615ca0684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c88cccaef550c4d3cde6f591d2fe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df545da4858de5af7705d69fba2707ab</data>
