    <node id="Classification Accuracy (CA)">
      <data key="d0">Classification Accuracy (CA)</data>
      <data key="d1">metric</data>
      <data key="d2">A metric defined in equation 3.1 and Table 3.2, used to evaluate the performance of classification, indicating the percentage of correctly classified instances.&lt;SEP&gt;A metric that measures the overall correctness of a model in classifying high-efficiency regions, calculated using components from a confusion matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Classification Accuracy (CA) is a metric calculated from the confusion matrix, indicating the percentage of correctly classified regions in an efficiency map.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-852a5b40a3022884df146775f2a7b320&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ce70f04fc1f66c450a145e83381de84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b</data>
