    <node id="Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)">
      <data key="d0">Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A CNN is a type of artificial neural network often used in image recognition and processing, here used within a variant of the sub-network.&lt;SEP&gt;A CNN is a type of Deep Learning model specifically designed for processing image data, characterized by its use of convolutional layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of neural network often used in image processing, where dropout can be applied to its filter's weights.&lt;SEP&gt;A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a type of deep learning architecture frequently used in the surveyed papers for Topology Optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da0a01577276faacfde89d458d90e662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3676b77d4e3057ccce502057364cbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-289a72546a02d10d2aa4147957dfa515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)">
      <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A RNN is a class of artificial neural networks where connections between nodes form a directed graph along a temporal sequence, used here in conjunction with a CNN.&lt;SEP&gt;A Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) is a type of neural network used with an attention mechanism in Figure 3.8(a) for encoding long-term dependencies and processing input sequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0dd4b73a53d12770e110415d865cc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289366</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Class Imbalance">
      <data key="d0">Class Imbalance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Class imbalance refers to situations where the number of examples in different classes is not equivalent, which is noted as not an issue for this analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where the number of instances in different classes is significantly unequal, which was not considered an issue for this analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-852a5b40a3022884df146775f2a7b320&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289432</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Surrogate Model">
      <data key="d0">Surrogate Model</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A model that can predict performance maps, reducing computational cost.&lt;SEP&gt;A surrogate model is an alternative model developed to accurately evaluate and/or optimize a device, especially when computationally expensive methods like FEA are impractical.&lt;SEP&gt;A surrogate model is a model of a model, typically a simplified model that approximates the behavior of a more complex model or system, used here for generating efficiency maps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb0bf44fcf7466c35982fd3bb8ae7ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b69dc7913a240aef52b550d176029b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285575</data>
    </node>
