    <node id="V-Design Cycle">
      <data key="d0">V-Design Cycle</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The V-design cycle, or VDC, is a common flow of product development that includes design, optimization, manufacturing, and test stages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electric Motors">
      <data key="d0">Electric Motors</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Devices with a product development process consisting of design and manufacturing stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Devices that convert electrical energy into mechanical energy.&lt;SEP&gt;These are devices whose acoustic noise prediction is studied using the surrogate-based method.&lt;SEP&gt;Devices used as context for the application of FEM.&lt;SEP&gt;Electric motors are the subject of the performance map calculations, focusing on their efficiency and power factor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ce41e8cc5ef38832503f503eebaccf56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fda188f6e0be572dc98e8f2a6ca4e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2e27a9a79daf5a813690efa01766eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-588116b5242516d003d1e70d48a7f42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
