    </node>
    <node id="Multiphysics Performance">
      <data key="d0">Multiphysics Performance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multiphysics performance refers to the analysis of various physical aspects of a design, evaluated using sophisticated simulation and design optimization tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285615</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FE Packages">
      <data key="d0">FE Packages</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">FE packages are sophisticated simulation and design optimization tools used to analyze multiphysics performances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conventional Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Conventional Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Conventional techniques are methods of analysis that involve massive computational burdens, making it infeasible to rank all possibilities for an optimal solution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Mining">
      <data key="d0">Data Mining</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Data mining involves the use of tools to analyze large datasets for patterns and information, along with Big Data, AI, and ML.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modern Machine Learning Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Modern Machine Learning Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Modern machine learning techniques, such as deep learning carried out with high-performance computing, are a focus of this work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Global Quantities">
      <data key="d0">Global Quantities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Global quantities, such as torque ripple, are design parameters with a limited number of output values for each motor design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fully Connected Neural Networks">
      <data key="d0">Fully Connected Neural Networks</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fully connected neural networks are a type of neural network that can lose attraction in many input-many output design and modeling problems due to training complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-610e0748724855c847b8fd20690e22db</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285616</data>
    </node>
