    <node id="Synchronous Reluctance Motor">
      <data key="d0">Synchronous Reluctance Motor</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is an object for which Topology Optimization results are presented (GA results with SeqTO-v1 and TD-Learning results).&lt;SEP&gt;A Synchronous Reluctance Motor is a type of electric motor whose rotor is discussed as an example for validating a method.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of motor whose rotor undergoes topology optimization using the level set method and shape design sensitivity.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of electric motor whose rotor is designed to maximize reluctance torque by manipulating magnetic reluctance paths.&lt;SEP&gt;A Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is a type of electrical machine whose geometric and electrical specifications are defined by fixed parameters for topology optimization experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is a type of electric motor that achieves torque through magnetic reluctance. It is the subject of the optimization study.&lt;SEP&gt;A Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is the subject of the design optimization, with its rotor geometry and magnetic flux distribution being analyzed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e2e27a9a79daf5a813690efa01766eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5a390cc7143789eccd25f5f3623694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5072e2b75e9621e87c85e7af0ee60311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ad9a81904dfb8134371112a0be9fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7b73719952876f4f9c0e6b4efe0027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f519dcf3231dec106e81c35523ed6914&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0011b0a6062b8a1499810eced96d7d94</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288942</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Evolutionary Algorithm-Based Discrete TO">
      <data key="d0">Evolutionary Algorithm-Based Discrete TO</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An evolutionary algorithm-based discrete Topology Optimization (TO) method, which benefits from reduced computational burden due to generalization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51ad9a81904dfb8134371112a0be9fa9</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discretized Design Space">
      <data key="d0">Discretized Design Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The space in which the sequence based controller moves, with cells serving as pointers.&lt;SEP&gt;The discretized design space is defined as a 5x5 grid, resulting in 25 cells (m=25), allowing for granular control over material distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51ad9a81904dfb8134371112a0be9fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0011b0a6062b8a1499810eced96d7d94</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288993</data>
    </node>
