      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Solution of the System of Equations is the fourth step in Finite Element Analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mesh Elements">
      <data key="d0">Mesh Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mesh elements are a primary factor for accuracy in finite element analysis models, especially in highly saturated regions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LU Decomposition">
      <data key="d0">LU Decomposition</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LU Decomposition is a numerical method for obtaining field solutions, used to reduce error between an estimate and the unknown solution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285652</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Banded Choleski">
      <data key="d0">Banded Choleski</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Banded Choleski is a numerical method for obtaining field solutions, used to reduce error between an estimate and the unknown solution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285652</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conjugate Gradient Method">
      <data key="d0">Conjugate Gradient Method</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Conjugate Gradient Method is a numerical method for obtaining field solutions, used to reduce error between an estimate and the unknown solution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285652</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient Method">
      <data key="d0">Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient Method</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient Method is a numerical method for obtaining field solutions, used to reduce error between an estimate and the unknown solution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
