    <node id="Lumped Parameter Models">
      <data key="d0">Lumped Parameter Models</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Lumped Parameter Models are less refined than Magnetic Equivalent Circuit models and do not account for machine geometry and material characteristics as thoroughly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Permeance Network Models">
      <data key="d0">Permeance Network Models</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Permeance network models are the basis for Magnetic Equivalent Circuits, comprising reluctance and magnetomotive force sources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285654</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MMF Sources">
      <data key="d0">MMF Sources</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MMF sources are currents flowing in the windings of an electric machine, which are placed in the teeth of the magnetic equivalent circuit.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetomotive force (MMF) sources are elements appearing in Magnetic Equivalent Circuit permeance network models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05d9b6a613299c6224fd2160377cbc33</data>
