    <node id="Ghorbanian and Lowther (2017)">
      <data key="d0">Ghorbanian and Lowther (2017)</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ghorbanian and Lowther (2017) are researchers cited for their contributions to the development of alternative surrogate models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electrical Circuit Description">
      <data key="d0">Electrical Circuit Description</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An electrical circuit description is the output of a reduced order FE method that translates the geometrical description of a magnetic device.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quasi-Stationary Device">
      <data key="d0">Quasi-Stationary Device</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An electric machine is assumed to be a quasi-stationary device, meaning any change in current that builds flux is followed by an immediate change of flux.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reluctance/Permeance">
      <data key="d0">Reluctance/Permeance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reluctance/permeance is a property assigned to each yoke part or tooth in the magnetic equivalent circuit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unknown Flux">
      <data key="d0">Unknown Flux</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Unknown flux is a parameter assigned to each yoke part or tooth in the magnetic equivalent circuit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Leakage Permeances">
      <data key="d0">Leakage Permeances</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Leakage permeances are used to model slots in the magnetic equivalent circuit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Air-Gap Flux Tube">
      <data key="d0">Air-Gap Flux Tube</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An air-gap flux tube is defined when any stator teeth come face to face with a rotor tooth, and permeance is assigned to it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Air-Gap Asymmetry">
      <data key="d0">Air-Gap Asymmetry</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Air-gap asymmetry refers to variations in the air-gap length between stator and rotor teeth, which affects the height of flux tubes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Motion in Motors">
      <data key="d0">Motion in Motors</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Motion in motors involves the change of a reluctance network, which adds complexity to solving equations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Comparison Between MEC &amp; FEA">
      <data key="d0">Comparison Between MEC &amp; FEA</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the comparison of Magnetic Equivalent Circuit method and Finite Element Analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Faults">
      <data key="d0">Internal Faults</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal faults are complex issues in machines that can be studied using FE analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Localized Magnetic Saturation">
      <data key="d0">Localized Magnetic Saturation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Localized magnetic saturation is a complex issue in machines that can be studied using FE analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computational Capability">
      <data key="d0">Computational Capability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Computational capability refers to the available resources for processing complex models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Final Design Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Final Design Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Final design analysis is the stage where FEA models are used after initial design stages, especially with limited computational capability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reduced Model Complexity">
      <data key="d0">Reduced Model Complexity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reduced model complexity is an advantage of the MEC method compared to FE methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285754</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ease of Parameterization">
      <data key="d0">Ease of Parameterization</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ease of parameterization is an advantage of the MEC method.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285754</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fast Computational Time">
      <data key="d0">Fast Computational Time</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fast computational time is an advantage of the MEC method.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Performance Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MEC is useful for performance analysis of devices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Initial Device Sizing">
      <data key="d0">Initial Device Sizing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MEC is useful for initial device sizing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complex Geometric Shapes">
      <data key="d0">Complex Geometric Shapes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Complex geometric shapes are a limitation for accurate representation by the MEC method.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Table 2.1">
      <data key="d0">Table 2.1</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 2.1 shows a comparison of reported results between FEA and MEC simulations against experimental measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2.1 is titled 'Experimental and Simulation result comparison' and presents a comparison of force and torque estimations from Finite Element Analysis (FEA) and Magnetic Equivalent Circuit (MEC) methods against experimental results in various electric machine studies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d146c06d89d470b7db435c475826c0e7</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289236</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experimental Measurements">
      <data key="d0">Experimental Measurements</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Experimental measurements are used as a benchmark to compare the accuracy of FEA and MEC simulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Experimental measurements are empirical data used as a baseline for comparison with simulation results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d146c06d89d470b7db435c475826c0e7</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289241</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployment Time for Simulation">
      <data key="d0">Deployment Time for Simulation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployment time for simulation refers to the time required to set up and run a simulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285755</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flexible Tool">
      <data key="d0">Flexible Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FEA is considered a more flexible tool for studying designs incorporating new shapes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Optimal Design">
      <data key="d0">Optimal Design</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Generating an optimal design often requires thousands of analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;The design that yields the highest performance value, achieved with a 1x1 controller on a SeqTO-vl environment for a force of 55 N.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimal Design refers to the best design obtained through various optimization methods, such as A2C and GA.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimal design refers to the most effective geometry or configuration found by the algorithms, aiming to maximize force generation.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of finding the best possible design solution given a set of constraints and objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimal design refers to a desired state or configuration whose behavior is understood through the visual representation of the graph under specific excitation values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b98982b6cac8028635bf8c32451b12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2c2f32fec14ff1bde53b19699374993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526ac278068ab9cbf72c11fd3817672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-588116b5242516d003d1e70d48a7f42c</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D-Q Analysis">
      <data key="d0">D-Q Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">D-Q analysis is a method used for shortlisting designs before testing with 3-D FEA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Computationally Expensive Process">
      <data key="d0">Computationally Expensive Process</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employing FE methods for modeling and simulation is a computationally expensive process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-592244534b4a5f40cf1d7d58a26d28cc</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285757</data>
    </node>
