      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Finite Element (FE) simulations are a computationally expensive method used to generate performance maps, which can take hours to days.&lt;SEP&gt;Finite Element (FE) simulations are traditional methods used to generate ground truth (target) efficiency maps, serving as a basis for evaluating the neural network model.</data>
