    <node id="CO2 Emission">
      <data key="d0">CO2 Emission</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CO2 emission refers to the carbon dioxide released into the atmosphere, with electrical machines estimated to contribute about 6040 Mega-tonnes globally.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285889</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Energy Efficiency">
      <data key="d0">Energy Efficiency</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Energy efficiency is crucial for energy conservation, environmental protection, and global sustainable development, and is a key objective in electric machine design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285890</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sustainable Development">
      <data key="d0">Sustainable Development</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sustainable development is a global concern that electric machine energy efficiency is crucial for.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285890</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Airbus A380 Droop Nose Ribs">
      <data key="d0">Airbus A380 Droop Nose Ribs</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Droop nose ribs are a component of the Airbus A380 designed using topology optimization to reduce weight while meeting mechanical performance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285890</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electrical Machines">
      <data key="d0">Electrical Machines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Electrical machines are core components in various appliances, industrial equipment, and systems, forming the foundation of the power industry and consuming a significant portion of global electricity.&lt;SEP&gt;Electrical Machines are the broader category of devices for which the neural network applications and motor design processes are being illustrated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-193c3a719cf23865bd32e0d110afb409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288833</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Physics Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Physics Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-physics analysis is a method used during the optimization process to investigate various engineering disciplines for each design option.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d168f1b6a8020e0606ef52cd19390</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285890</data>
    </node>
