    <node id="ML Or DL Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">ML Or DL Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Machine Learning or Deep Learning algorithms, which are budding areas of research with applications in various fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b36856e6868820792611d3fddfdfc66f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Epsilon">
      <data key="d0">Epsilon</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Epsilon is a parameter in the epsilon-greedy method that represents the agent's probability of choosing to explore over exploit.&lt;SEP&gt;A scalar parameter between 0 and 1, representing the probability of choosing a random action, which controls the trade-off between exploration and exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;Epsilon is a probability value (1 - epsilon or epsilon) that determines the likelihood of choosing an action based on Argmax or a random action.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-023a66b0b7b2235f3cc11df422f013f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9242b5eeb7a8558a1b50bf53c2ccacba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292901</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MDPs (Markov Decision Processes)">
      <data key="d0">MDPs (Markov Decision Processes)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MDPs are a mathematical framework for modeling decision making in situations where outcomes are partly random and partly under the control of a decision maker.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pure Iron">
      <data key="d0">Pure Iron</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Pure iron is a linear material with linear B-H characteristics used in the C-core topology optimization study.&lt;SEP&gt;The material of the C-core, which is described as exhibiting linear B-H characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb64932da4baf92322bc61ecf0df44f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conventional C-core EM Actuator">
      <data key="d0">Conventional C-core EM Actuator</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A conventional C-core EM actuator is a device that experiences a force of 40 N on its armature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Armature Force">
      <data key="d0">Armature Force</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Armature force is the force experienced by the armature of an electromagnetic actuator.&lt;SEP&gt;Armature force is a key performance metric, measured in Newtons (N), presented in the C-core results and compared between different optimization methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af2139266a69c7c4fede66d615ca0684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Greedy Action">
      <data key="d0">Greedy Action</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A greedy action is chosen by an agent to try and get the most reward based on current estimated values.&lt;SEP&gt;The greedy action is the action $a$ that yields the maximum Q-value for the current state $s$ at time $t$, derived from the $\\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$ operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289379</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Random Action">
      <data key="d0">Random Action</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A random action is chosen with probability epsilon during exploration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Epsilon Value">
      <data key="d0">Epsilon Value</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The epsilon value is a parameter that determines the probability of an agent choosing to explore over exploit, ranging from 0 to 1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Optimal Deterministic Policy">
      <data key="d0">Optimal Deterministic Policy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An optimal deterministic policy is a policy in MDPs that is better than any other policy.&lt;SEP&gt;An optimal deterministic policy is a strategy, derived from an optimal Q-function, that prescribes the single best action for every possible state to maximize future rewards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-146167a8b3388ece49f9a67ad320dd0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exploration-Exploitation Dilemma">
      <data key="d0">Exploration-Exploitation Dilemma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The exploration-exploitation dilemma arises when agents must choose between exploring new actions or exploiting known good actions to maximize reward.&lt;SEP&gt;A challenge in reinforcement learning that Q-Learning addresses by balancing exploring new actions and exploiting known good actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The exploration-exploitation dilemma is the challenge of balancing the need to explore new actions to discover better rewards with the need to exploit known actions that yield high rewards.&lt;SEP&gt;The exploration-exploitation dilemma is a fundamental problem in reinforcement learning that involves choosing between exploring new actions and exploiting known good actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-023a66b0b7b2235f3cc11df422f013f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e759e174fdc4ef458e871149c5bf316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High Dimensionality State-Space">
      <data key="d0">High Dimensionality State-Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A high dimensionality state-space is an environment where the number of possible states is very large, making exhaustive exploration difficult.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MDP Representation">
      <data key="d0">MDP Representation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MDP representation refers to the use of Markov Decision Processes to model an environment, often involving field value in the state representation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electrical Steel (M-19 26 Ga)">
      <data key="d0">Electrical Steel (M-19 26 Ga)</data>
      <data key="d1">material</data>
      <data key="d2">Electrical Steel (M-19 26 Ga) is a nonlinear material used in the C-core topology optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ON/OFF Based TO Algorithm">
      <data key="d0">ON/OFF Based TO Algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An ON/OFF based TO algorithm is a topology optimization algorithm that employs electrical steel, used by Midha et al. (2019) and Park and Min (2009a).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Processing Filters">
      <data key="d0">Post-Processing Filters</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-processing filters are applied to enforce topology smoothness after an algorithm such as ON/OFF based TO.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e1757cd493f052e1f9528255eb34ea59</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760285977</data>
    </node>
