    <node id="Dense Layers">
      <data key="d0">Dense Layers</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Two layers in the network architecture following the convolutional layer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286008</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Critic Network">
      <data key="d0">Critic Network</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Part of the Actor-Critic model, its output layer is dense and used for regression.&lt;SEP&gt;The Critic Network is a component of the Actor-Critic framework responsible for estimating the value function, specifically the Q-value network, to provide feedback to the Actor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Critic network is one of the two distinct output pathways of the A2C network, producing a Value Function output of 1 x 1 dimension.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5dae035c707962e5992f8ffb5b5c0c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298487c8d447bf081bcb2234cb4ddb80</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288791</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Actor Network">
      <data key="d0">Actor Network</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Part of the Actor-Critic model, its output layer uses Softmax for distinct classes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actor Network is a component of the Actor-Critic framework responsible for learning and adjusting the policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actor network is the second distinct output pathway of the A2C network, producing an output with a dimension of 1 x 8, representing a probability distribution over eight possible actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5dae035c707962e5992f8ffb5b5c0c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298487c8d447bf081bcb2234cb4ddb80</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288791</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Input Multi-Output Network">
      <data key="d0">Single Input Multi-Output Network</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A network configuration formed by merging Actor and Critic functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cc8202063f67533ab2523d99cadd60f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286008</data>
    </node>
