    <node id="Maxwell's Equations">
      <data key="d0">Maxwell's Equations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maxwell's equations are a set of partial differential equations that, together with the Lorentz force law, form the foundation of classical electromagnetism, classical optics, and electric circuits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Modeling is the mathematical representation of physical phenomena.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286012</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Simulation">
      <data key="d0">Simulation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Simulation is the numerical representation of models on computing machines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electromagnetic Modeling and Simulation">
      <data key="d0">Electromagnetic Modeling and Simulation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">This field involves the process of representing electromagnetic phenomena and simulating them, broadly divided into Analytical, Numerical, and Magnetic Equivalent Circuits algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Analytical Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Analytical Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Analytical algorithms are a category of electromagnetic modeling algorithms that are computationally less demanding and provide faster results by seeking closed-form expressions for magnetic fields and losses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Numerical Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Numerical Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Numerical algorithms are a category of algorithms for electromagnetic modeling and simulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetic Equivalent Circuits (MEC)">
      <data key="d0">Magnetic Equivalent Circuits (MEC)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Magnetic Equivalent Circuits (MEC) is a modeling method primarily used in electric machines, which can be considered analytical or numerical depending on its application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Finite Element (FE) Method">
      <data key="d0">Finite Element (FE) Method</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Finite Element (FE) method, implemented in software suites, allows for accurate 3D analysis of electric machines with coupled fields and is currently preferred by machine designers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Finite Difference Methods (FDM)">
      <data key="d0">Finite Difference Methods (FDM)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Finite Difference Methods (FDM) are another option to model electric machines but have difficulties with complex geometries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74285f9f1c2db4a1aaef011e90f166c0</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286013</data>
    </node>
