    <node id="Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM)">
      <data key="d0">Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM)</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is an electric machine whose rotor is optimized using the proposed TO methodology, known for high efficiency and power density.&lt;SEP&gt;Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) is the subject of the design and analysis, specifically its rotor.&lt;SEP&gt;A SynRM (Synchronous Reluctance Motor) is the subject of a Topology Optimization experiment, where its design is optimized using TD-learning with SeqTO-v1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b7b73719952876f4f9c0e6b4efe0027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5526ac278068ab9cbf72c11fd3817672</data>
