    <node id="Origin">
      <data key="d0">Origin</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6dd34d919cd23617da046186d8e9bc3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d2">Losing a life places the controller (agent) back at the origin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Origin is a small black filled circle in the bottom-left corner of the Fixed Air Box, serving as the reference point for the coordinate system.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288926</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetic Material">
      <data key="d0">Magnetic Material</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2c2f32fec14ff1bde53b19699374993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c48c238aedc178e88e075043138eb72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d2">After losing a life and returning to the origin, the agent adds magnetic material where the design is affected by magnetic saturation.&lt;SEP&gt;The agent adds magnetic material in a region where saturation is severe.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic material refers to the solid dark blue areas of the C-core, acting as a high-permeability path for magnetic flux.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic material, likely iron or steel, is represented by blue cells in the optimal geometry diagrams.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic material, typically shown in blue cells, is a component of the optimal geometry used to conduct magnetic flux.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288864</data>
    </node>
