      <data key="d0">Magnetic Field</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31fcb301590d668517d7e9583a508d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c8eeb9e91e5bd71f6909085d5d4a52e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2785b4e150ada39f3077e573325eeb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ad9a81904dfb8134371112a0be9fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb64932da4baf92322bc61ecf0df44f</data>
      <data key="d2">The current-carrying coil produces a magnetic field according to Ampere’s Circuit Law.&lt;SEP&gt;An invisible force field generated by the Coils that affects the Armature.&lt;SEP&gt;The Magnetic Field, denoted by |B|, is influenced or measured in the region of the Air Gap, consistent with an electromagnetic problem.&lt;SEP&gt;The magnetic field is induced by the coils within the C-core and acts upon the armature.&lt;SEP&gt;The magnetic field properties, represented by B distribution, are a key aspect of the analysis.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289114</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electromagnet">
      <data key="d0">Electromagnet</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51ad9a81904dfb8134371112a0be9fa9</data>
