      <data key="d3">chunk-ca632ae39508b7c6fdf1ad04973857b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb622c9ce0600f3539c3ed7199e0c0ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03395909e238b7701943add27146739b</data>
      <data key="d2">The terminology of an N-layer neural network does not count the input layer.&lt;SEP&gt;The Input Layer is the leftmost element of the neural network diagram, enclosed in a light red rounded rectangle, containing three circular nodes labeled 'I₁', 'I₂', and 'I₃'.&lt;SEP&gt;The Input Layer is the initial component of the Feedforward Neural Network, composed of shaded circular nodes (`I1, I2, I3, In`) that receive the State or State-action pair. It can accommodate 'n' input features.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288964</data>
    </node>
