      <data key="d3">chunk-de8952c3b21b80d4712abc62f00e8c46</data>
      <data key="d2">Uncertainty maps can provide a qualitative measure.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bayesian Inference">
      <data key="d0">Bayesian Inference</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de8952c3b21b80d4712abc62f00e8c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd6ce2b178e669e439db6c5cb7f00f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92cc2b02ae3a119d92f0d1a7f6617885&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c2729bc0700da0250623cae161a1895</data>
      <data key="d2">Dropout can be cast as approximate Bayesian inference over the network’s weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian Inference is a statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more relevant evidence or information becomes available.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian Inference is the process of quantifying updated beliefs about model parameters (weights) after observing new evidence (training data), using Bayes' Theorem.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian Inference is a statistical method used to process magnetic field prediction results, particularly in generating uncertainty maps.</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Standard Deviation Of Monte Carlo Samples">
      <data key="d0">Standard Deviation Of Monte Carlo Samples</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de8952c3b21b80d4712abc62f00e8c46</data>
      <data key="d2">The standard deviation of Monte Carlo samples is related to classification accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760286990</data>
    </node>
