    <node id="Agent-Environment Interaction">
      <data key="d0">Agent-Environment Interaction</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5c17ed6446ce59a36ae88843222657c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906a75be5f88ad37713839d335d1720c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28d95920dc2d89112c02d6c86f6d7e2</data>
      <data key="d2">The agent-environment interaction generates a trajectory of experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Agent-environment interaction describes how agents in reinforcement learning learn by interacting with their surroundings.&lt;SEP&gt;Agent-Environment Interaction describes the process where an agent takes actions in an environment, and the environment responds with new states and rewards.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289192</data>
    </node>
