    </node>
    <node id="Policy Network">
      <data key="d0">Policy Network</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b6b9bf681c07677d8af5a26068c52f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7133594b2e19b403575b42aef1cafffb</data>
      <data key="d2">The learning rate (α) is used in the change of the weights of the policy network.&lt;SEP&gt;A Policy Network is a neural network that defines the policy π, whose parameters θ are updated during the learning process.&lt;SEP&gt;A policy network, also known as the actor, is a component in reinforcement learning algorithms that determines the agent's actions based on the current state.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288806</data>
    </node>
