    <node id="Advantage Actor-Critic">
      <data key="d0">Advantage Actor-Critic</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22c061c45c3a0d2579ced8d3121f0d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e3e1dd6f2a21d7997b5fa281b76b709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298487c8d447bf081bcb2234cb4ddb80</data>
      <data key="d2">Advantage Actor-Critic algorithms replace the Q-value with 'Advantage' as a performance metric.&lt;SEP&gt;Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C) is an advanced reinforcement learning algorithm that refines the Actor-Critic framework by incorporating the Advantage function.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C) algorithm is an extension of the Actor-Critic framework that utilizes the Advantage function for improved policy updates, specifically requiring an agent to learn only the State-Value Function.</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288818</data>
    </node>
