    <node id="SeqTO-v1 with GA">
      <data key="d0">SeqTO-v1 with GA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SeqTO-v1 with GA is an optimization method (Sequential Topology Optimization with Genetic Algorithm) used to achieve the optimized geometry.&lt;SEP&gt;SeqTO-v1 with GA is an optimization method used to determine the optimized geometry in a non-linear environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0691c9f7251ff59c05b1bc277ea93e1</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288860</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3x3 Linear Environment">
      <data key="d0">3x3 Linear Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The 3x3 Linear Environment describes the specific conditions and controller size (3x3) under which the C-core electromagnet's geometry was optimized.&lt;SEP&gt;This refers to the specific setup or context in which the magnetic field distribution is optimized, likely indicating a matrix or grid configuration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb64932da4baf92322bc61ecf0df44f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Shaded Plot |B| smoothed">
      <data key="d0">Shaded Plot |B| smoothed</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Shaded Plot |B| smoothed is a legend indicating the representation of the magnitude of the magnetic field strength, using a color gradient.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flux Lines">
      <data key="d0">Flux Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Flux lines are thin, black lines, some solid and some dashed, overlaid on the shaded plot, representing the direction and density of the magnetic flux.&lt;SEP&gt;Flux lines are visual representations overlaid on B-distribution plots, indicating the direction and density of the magnetic field.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-081d5d2ff62504474fc8532dd817fb39</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetic Field Strength">
      <data key="d0">Magnetic Field Strength</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Magnetic Field Strength is the key performance indicator for the C-core, substituting the noisy force value and is being optimized.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic field strength is a physical quantity represented by a color gradient in the visualization, ranging from 0 to 6.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31fcb301590d668517d7e9583a508d90</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288861</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Color Gradient">
      <data key="d0">Color Gradient</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A color gradient from red to dark blue is used to represent the magnitude of the magnetic field strength, with red indicating strong fields and dark blue indicating weak fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288863</data>
    </node>
