    </node>
    <node id="High-Permeability Path">
      <data key="d0">High-Permeability Path</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-permeability path describes the function of the C-core's magnetic material in guiding the magnetic flux.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288865</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C-Core Topology Optimization">
      <data key="d0">C-Core Topology Optimization</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">C-core topology optimization is a design process result to achieve an efficient magnetic core structure, confirmed by the image context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d8330ecbeee1c4ebe7ea64bfd7fbb45b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288865</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mathematical Equation">
      <data key="d0">Mathematical Equation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The provided equation defines a binary material distribution based on the sign of a level set function.&lt;SEP&gt;The equation presented is a sequence of state-action pairs and their corresponding action-value function estimates under a specific policy, illustrating a trajectory within a Reinforcement Learning (RL) context.&lt;SEP&gt;The equation {\\mathrm { T r a i n i n g } } \\Longrightarrow \\theta \\longrightarrow \\pi symbolically represents the process by which a policy is learned and refined through training in Policy Gradient algorithms.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical equation represents an updating rule for a parameter theta, involving a learning rate alpha and the gradient of a cost function J.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9a600bc388389f7228161e154b865877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d40236fe707c1436e66df73317598df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ac9217313164d00979e7afd6541254</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Theta ($\theta$)">
      <data key="d0">Theta ($\theta$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Theta ($\theta$) denotes the parameters (weights) of the neural network in Policy Gradient, which are adjusted during the learning process to optimize the policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Theta ($\theta$) represents parameters within the equation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f94c2e92a45229c63d7fd85dceb68356&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pi ($\pi$)">
      <data key="d0">Pi ($\pi$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pi ($\pi$) represents the policy in Reinforcement Learning, mapping states to actions or a probability distribution over actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pi ($\pi$) represents a policy, which defines the actions to be taken in certain states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f94c2e92a45229c63d7fd85dceb68356&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Measure J($\theta$)">
      <data key="d0">Performance Measure J($\theta$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The performance measure J($\theta$) is an objective function that the training process aims to maximize with respect to $\theta$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288867</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Learning Rate Alpha ($\alpha$)">
      <data key="d0">Learning Rate Alpha ($\alpha$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The learning rate alpha ($\alpha$) is a hyperparameter that dictates the step size of updates to $\theta$ during training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288867</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Probability of Action Selection p(a)">
      <data key="d0">Probability of Action Selection p(a)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The probability of action selection p(a) is determined by the policy ($\pi$), which is often a stochastic distribution over actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288867</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameters (Weights)">
      <data key="d0">Parameters (Weights)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters (weights) are the trainable components of a neural network, denoted by $\theta$, adjusted during learning to optimize the policy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Go">
      <data key="d0">Go</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Go is a practical application or use case for Policy Gradient algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1cc3c9a8202b9032fe06ba473d7c76d8</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760288868</data>
    </node>
