      <data key="d0">Sequential Topology Optimization - Reinforcement Learning (SeqTO-RL)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Sequential Topology Optimization - Reinforcement Learning (SeqTO-RL) is an optimization methodology for designing an electromagnetic actuator, represented in row (c) of Figure 5.21.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C-Core Solenoid">
      <data key="d0">C-Core Solenoid</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The C-core solenoid is a specific type of electromagnetic actuator whose optimal geometry and magnetic field distribution are analyzed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Air/Non-Magnetic Material">
      <data key="d0">Air/Non-Magnetic Material</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Air or non-magnetic material is represented by white cells in the optimal geometry panels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sequential Topology Optimization - Q-Learning">
      <data key="d0">Sequential Topology Optimization - Q-Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Sequential Topology Optimization - Q-Learning (SeqTO-QL) is an optimization methodology used for designing an electromagnetic actuator, specifically a C-core solenoid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289048</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sequential Topology Optimization - Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d0">Sequential Topology Optimization - Reinforcement Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Sequential Topology Optimization - Reinforcement Learning (SeqTO-RL) is an optimization methodology used for designing an electromagnetic actuator, specifically a C-core solenoid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289048</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Magnetic Material">
      <data key="d0">Non-Magnetic Material</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-magnetic material, referred to as air, is represented by white cells in the optimal geometry diagrams.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289048</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coil Windings">
      <data key="d0">Coil Windings</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Coil windings are electric coils, represented by textured orange rectangular blocks, positioned on the C-core solenoid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b984e4831b11f20f84bb8669cd7396b</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Algorithm Optimization">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Algorithm Optimization</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic Algorithm optimization is a method for which the C-core actuator and its components serve as an example of application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coordinate System">
      <data key="d0">Coordinate System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Coordinate System is implied by the dimensions X7 and the 91.5mm fixed dimension, with its origin at the bottom-left of the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;A coordinate system (x and y axes) is visible in the diagram, indicating the orientation and symmetry along the x-axis, used to reduce the size of the design space.&lt;SEP&gt;A 2D coordinate system with X and Y axes and an origin is depicted in the bottom-left corner of the image, clarifying the 2D nature of the representation and the use of symmetry.&lt;SEP&gt;A small coordinate system in the bottom-left corner of the grid indicates the 'X' axis pointing right and the 'Y' axis pointing upwards.&lt;SEP&gt;A system used to define positions, present in the bottom left corner of both panels, with a green 'y' axis and a red 'x' axis.&lt;SEP&gt;A visual representation showing a green arrow for 'Y' and a red arrow for 'X', originating from a blue dot, providing spatial orientation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca13e3ef7d4bf929b84d6b30574e3485&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8803108c64e008ff20b50a70b77f8af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57172dfb9b0c90234ff04b1a5519b71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beaf090538cf5ed83b97d616d5275826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb64932da4baf92322bc61ecf0df44f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2D Cross-Sectional Diagram">
      <data key="d0">2D Cross-Sectional Diagram</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A 2D cross-sectional diagram is the visual representation of the C-Core EM Actuator, illustrating its components and dimensions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="X-Axis">
      <data key="d0">X-Axis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The X-axis is part of the coordinate system, represented by a dashed-dotted line, indicating a plane of symmetry for the C-Core EM actuator design.&lt;SEP&gt;The X-Axis is part of the coordinate system, indicated by a red arrow pointing to the right, signifying symmetry in the design space.&lt;SEP&gt;The X-axis runs horizontally in the coordinate system, representing one dimension of the 2D design space, and symmetry about it is utilized to reduce design space size.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57172dfb9b0c90234ff04b1a5519b71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26404cee26f7623e6d969e264821542f</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORE">
      <data key="d0">CORE</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The CORE is a C-shaped, gray, solid component of the C-core EM actuator, with a horizontal upper section and two vertical arms extending downwards.&lt;SEP&gt;The CORE is the main body of the C-core design, shaped like a 'C' and made of light gray material.&lt;SEP&gt;The CORE is a C-shaped component of the C-core actuator, made of dark gray material.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b83022ca44128f92a414d02c9b7fc66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca13e3ef7d4bf929b84d6b30574e3485</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Symmetry About The X-Axis">
      <data key="d0">Symmetry About The X-Axis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Symmetry about the x-axis is a technical detail utilized to reduce the size of the design space for optimization, represented by a dashed-dotted line in the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;Symmetry about the x-axis is utilized to reduce the size of the design space, allowing only half of the C-core to be modeled.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d94fd82540e01e83a3a7b0febcf3d7ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57172dfb9b0c90234ff04b1a5519b71e</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289050</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Table 4.7: SynRM Results Using TD-Learning with SeqTO-v1">
      <data key="d0">Table 4.7: SynRM Results Using TD-Learning with SeqTO-v1</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 4.7 presents the results of a Topology Optimization experiment on a Synchronous Reluctance Motor (SynRM) using TD-learning with SeqTO-v1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289051</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environment Type">
      <data key="d0">Environment Type</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Environment Type is a column header describing the configuration of the experimental environment for C-core optimization, including controller size and material type.&lt;SEP&gt;Environment Type specifies the design space for the SynRM rotor, which is a '5 × 5 (Non-linear)' discretized space.&lt;SEP&gt;The 'EnvironmentType' refers to the discretization of the design space, specified as '5 × 5 (Non-linear)' for the optimization problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5a390cc7143789eccd25f5f3623694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af2139266a69c7c4fede66d615ca0684</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289052</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Episode Length">
      <data key="d0">Episode Length</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Episode Length is a parameter in the TD-learning algorithm, reported as '25', corresponding to the number of elements in the design grid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289052</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5 × 5 (Non-Linear) Design Space">
      <data key="d0">5 × 5 (Non-Linear) Design Space</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The '5 × 5 (Non-linear)' design space refers to the discretized environmental type for the SynRM rotor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b6f3bea48fce928809f6ddf7db422c4</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760289052</data>
