      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292302</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Action $a$">
      <data key="d0">Action $a$</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d2">Random sampling is a procedure by which an action $a$ is selected from the set of all possible actions.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="$\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$">
      <data key="d0">$\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d2">The $\\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$ operator calculates the action $a$ that maximizes the Q-value for $Q_t(s, a)$.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292307</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Panel (B)">
      <data key="d0">Panel (B)</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca13e3ef7d4bf929b84d6b30574e3485</data>
      <data key="d2">Panel (b)'s discretized representation implies the use of a Finite Element Method for simulation.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Improved Prediction Accuracy">
      <data key="d0">Improved Prediction Accuracy</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da0a01577276faacfde89d458d90e662</data>
      <data key="d2">Monte Carlo sampling, an approximation of this integral, has been shown to improve classification accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292380</data>
    </node>
    <node id="p(y|x, X, Y) = Integral p(y|x, W) x p(W|X, Y) dW">
      <data key="d0">p(y|x, X, Y) = Integral p(y|x, W) x p(W|X, Y) dW</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da0a01577276faacfde89d458d90e662</data>
      <data key="d2">The Equation is defined as p(y|x, X, Y) = Integral p(y|x, W) x p(W|X, Y) dW.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292380</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q-learning with Function Approximation">
