    <node id="True Positives (TP)">
      <data key="d0">True Positives (TP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">True Positives (TP) refer to instances where the model correctly predicted the positive class.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a6871b523f5d81edec8c74e56e7c813</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="True Negatives (TN)">
      <data key="d0">True Negatives (TN)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">True Negatives (TN) refer to instances where the model correctly predicted the negative class.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a6871b523f5d81edec8c74e56e7c813</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="False Positives (FP)">
      <data key="d0">False Positives (FP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">False Positives (FP) refer to instances where the model incorrectly predicted the positive class when the actual class was negative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a6871b523f5d81edec8c74e56e7c813</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="False Negatives (FN)">
      <data key="d0">False Negatives (FN)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">False Negatives (FN) refer to instances where the model incorrectly predicted the negative class when the actual class was positive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a6871b523f5d81edec8c74e56e7c813</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Next Action (a')">
      <data key="d0">Next Action (a')</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Next Action (a') represents a possible action in the next state s' that maximizes the Q-value in the Q-Learning equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Next Action (a') represents a potential action in the next state s_{t+1}, used to find the maximum Q-value for that state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c9121d5ef96392cd935214b547cd6dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8823695e17798553515e243bdbfda2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292784</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LaTeX">
      <data key="d0">LaTeX</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">LaTeX is a document preparation system and markup language predominantly used for high-quality typesetting, particularly for academic and scientific content. It is widely applied for formatting documents that include mathematical formulas, equations, and diverse scientific material, such as scientific texts and technical documentation. Its primary strength lies in its ability to present complex mathematical and scientific information precisely and professionally. This makes it an essential tool for academic papers, books, and other documents requiring specialized formatting, specifically for rendering or formatting mathematical equations and representing them accurately.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system often used for typesetting mathematical equations.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system used for typesetting, especially for mathematical and scientific documents, indicating the format of the equation.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system used for typesetting, particularly for mathematical and scientific expressions.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system used for typesetting, especially for mathematical and scientific content.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system used to represent the equation in a structured format.&lt;SEP&gt;LaTeX is a document preparation system used for typesetting, particularly for mathematical and scientific documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86d0a1a94798eb7b1674502b0ae73cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8823695e17798553515e243bdbfda2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0e0689a5d95559de772960193f788e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e280b998ddabea3a4713c685bb83d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ac9217313164d00979e7afd6541254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec4e495c59f004fcbe4475de4b2bcbd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feffff69e0f56312f2846d9f57d0a4f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215b04d60447db6b473faf768914326f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9ed49570cc7fd3b04f001bb2371e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3c16dd3211cf28f9ec77da01f786ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b2d0224b72ce534931ab18bf45eae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f95cef6c8e603e27b162387295b8935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6cf4c742d5c3ecf6b0e985a5914f0f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19afc62597694db2255ea53cb7e6f242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-620c2ed72be858c05e569ae1452705a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9121d5ef96392cd935214b547cd6dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e5324f5a16fd6822c647598c8e749b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1035840471dadb1efd9b1057b1d2f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae820ad2360b2e0540cedd11e75bb15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2a1300fe0e15e6c2632ac8232faa468&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1039c6984ae2b3caedcb109bdc272a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c769a26f512a088ad02de1c81c6ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6444ddfe2f3b1042c888bb109eee4098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14506e8e02aeb799dcd49d4b24c5b529&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be1e8d82c79e97d6340503568a2610b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679341b128f5b4ef1cbba0b4763e7aa8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293131</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R_{t+1}">
      <data key="d0">R_{t+1}</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R_{t+1} is the first term in the summation sequence for G_t.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b2d0224b72ce534931ab18bf45eae47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R_{t+2}">
      <data key="d0">R_{t+2}</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R_{t+2} is the second term in the summation sequence for G_t.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b2d0224b72ce534931ab18bf45eae47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R_n">
      <data key="d0">R_n</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R_n represents a reward received at time n, which is the final reward in a sequence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b2d0224b72ce534931ab18bf45eae47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R">
      <data key="d0">R</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R is a variable used in the equation, indexed by t+1, t+2, and up to n.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4b2d0224b72ce534931ab18bf45eae47</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="nabla">
      <data key="d0">nabla</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nabla (∇) is a differential operator used in vector calculus.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-620c2ed72be858c05e569ae1452705a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="log">
      <data key="d0">log</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Logarithm (log) is a mathematical function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-620c2ed72be858c05e569ae1452705a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content">
      <data key="d0">Content</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed1035840471dadb1efd9b1057b1d2f9</data>
      <data key="d2">The mathematical expression is categorized as an Equation.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292721</data>
    </node>
    <node id="π (pi)">
      <data key="d0">π (pi)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">π (pi) represents a policy in reinforcement learning, which defines the probability of taking each action in each state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6444ddfe2f3b1042c888bb109eee4098</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KL Divergence">
      <data key="d0">KL Divergence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">KL Divergence is a mathematical equation representing the Kullback-Leibler divergence between a variational distribution q(W) and the true posterior distribution p(W|X, Y).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-916831dfb3bd404b7a6bf4cf512b41b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Variational Distribution q(W)">
      <data key="d0">Variational Distribution q(W)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The variational distribution q(W) is an approximation of the true posterior distribution in the context of KL Divergence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-916831dfb3bd404b7a6bf4cf512b41b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Posterior Distribution p(W|X, Y)">
      <data key="d0">Posterior Distribution p(W|X, Y)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The posterior distribution p(W|X, Y) is the true distribution of W given observed data X and labels Y.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-916831dfb3bd404b7a6bf4cf512b41b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="a^*">
      <data key="d0">a^*</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">a^*' is the optimal action or argument that maximizes the Q-function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f3c16dd3211cf28f9ec77da01f786ee6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q-hat Function">
      <data key="d0">Q-hat Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Q-hat function, denoted as $\hat{Q}(s_i, a_j, w)$, represents an estimated Q-value in the context of reinforcement learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="State $s_i$">
      <data key="d0">State $s_i$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The state $s_i$ is a specific state within a system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Action $a_j$">
      <data key="d0">Action $a_j$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The action $a_j$ is a specific action that can be taken within a system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Weight Vector $w$">
      <data key="d0">Weight Vector $w$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The weight vector $w$ is a set of weights used in the linear approximation of the Q-function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feature Vector $x(s_i, a_j)$">
      <data key="d0">Feature Vector $x(s_i, a_j)$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The feature vector $x(s_i, a_j)$ combines information about a specific state $s_i$ and action $a_j$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Weight Component $w_{ij}$">
      <data key="d0">Weight Component $w_{ij}$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The weight component $w_{ij}$ is a specific element from the weight vector $w$ that corresponds to the state-action pair $(s_i, a_j)$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q-Hat">
      <data key="d0">Q-Hat</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Q-Hat is an estimated Q-value function, denoted as $\hat{Q}$, which is approximated as a dot product of a weight vector and a state-action feature vector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="s_i">
      <data key="d0">s_i</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">s_i represents a specific state in a given context, often used in reinforcement learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292758</data>
    </node>
    <node id="a_j">
      <data key="d0">a_j</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">a_j represents a specific action in a given context, often used in reinforcement learning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="x(s_i, a_j)">
      <data key="d0">x(s_i, a_j)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">x(s_i, a_j) is a feature vector representing the state-action pair (s_i, a_j).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_ij">
      <data key="d0">w_ij</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">w_ij is a specific weight from the weight vector w that corresponds to the state-action pair (s_i, a_j), implying a lookup table form.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LaTeX Equation">
      <data key="d0">LaTeX Equation</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The LaTeX Equation is a mathematical expression presented in LaTeX format, defining the approximation of $\hat{Q}$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ab45d957d12b26323f8399b12bc7b9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="State-Action Value Function ($\hat{Q}$)">
      <data key="d0">State-Action Value Function ($\hat{Q}$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The state-action value function ($\hat{Q}$) estimates the expected return for taking action 'a' in state 's' under policy 'w'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="State ($s_t, s_{t+1}$)">
      <data key="d0">State ($s_t, s_{t+1}$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">State represents the current situation or environment at time t or t+1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Action ($a_t, a_{t+1}$)">
      <data key="d0">Action ($a_t, a_{t+1}$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Action represents a choice or step taken by an agent at time t or t+1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gradient ($\nabla \hat{Q}$)">
      <data key="d0">Gradient ($\nabla \hat{Q}$)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The gradient represents the direction and rate of steepest ascent of the state-action value function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292764</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Weight Vector Update Equation">
      <data key="d0">Weight Vector Update Equation</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">This is an equation for updating a weight vector 'w' in a reinforcement learning context, involving a learning rate alpha, a reward, and estimated Q-values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292764</data>
    </node>
    <node id="alpha">
      <data key="d0">alpha</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Representing the learning rate, denoted by the Greek letter $\alpha$.&lt;SEP&gt;The variable 'alpha' (α) is likely a learning rate parameter in the equation.&lt;SEP&gt;alpha likely represents a learning rate, a parameter that controls the step size in optimization algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb650db56653b515d55eb1ef7514257&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1039c6984ae2b3caedcb109bdc272a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Estimated Q-Value">
      <data key="d0">Estimated Q-Value</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Representing the estimated Q-value, denoted by $\hat{Q}$, which is a function of state, action, and weights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292764</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gradient of Estimated Q-Value">
      <data key="d0">Gradient of Estimated Q-Value</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Representing the gradient of the estimated Q-value with respect to the weights, denoted by $\nabla \hat{Q}$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WEIGHTS (W)">
      <data key="d0">WEIGHTS (W)</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-39c26f40d41eeedc15f07ee76f39c83c</data>
      <data key="d2">The equation shows how the weights (w) are updated.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Next State (s_{t+1})">
      <data key="d0">Next State (s_{t+1})</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Next State (s_{t+1}) is the state of the agent at the next time step, resulting from taking action a_t in state s_t.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a8823695e17798553515e243bdbfda2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292784</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Max Operator">
      <data key="d0">Max Operator</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The operator max a' selects the maximum Q-value over all possible next actions a'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a8823695e17798553515e243bdbfda2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="f(a)">
      <data key="d0">f(a)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The function 'f(a)' is the objective function that needs to be minimized in the optimization problem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14506e8e02aeb799dcd49d4b24c5b529</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="i">
      <data key="d0">i</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">i is an index variable, with different ranges specified in the context of the equation (i=0,1,2,3 or i=0,1,2,...,m).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14506e8e02aeb799dcd49d4b24c5b529</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="j">
      <data key="d0">j</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">j is an index variable, ranging from 1 to n in the summation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14506e8e02aeb799dcd49d4b24c5b529</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="m">
      <data key="d0">m</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">m is a variable representing an upper limit for the index 'i'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14506e8e02aeb799dcd49d4b24c5b529</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Qπ(st, at)">
      <data key="d0">Qπ(st, at)</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">This notation represents the approximation or estimation of the Q-value for a given state 'st' and action 'at' under policy 'π'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a8823695e17798553515e243bdbfda2</data>
