    <node id="Squared Difference">
      <data key="d0">Squared Difference</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The squared difference is a mathematical operation used in the calculation of Error (MSE) to quantify the discrepancy between two values.&lt;SEP&gt;The squared difference between Q-Pi(s,a) and Q-Hat(s,a,w) is a common error term or loss function used in optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19afc62597694db2255ea53cb7e6f242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293067</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q*(s,a)">
      <data key="d0">Q*(s,a)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Q*(s,a) represents the optimal Q-value for a given state (s) and action (a).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q^(s,a,w)">
      <data key="d0">Q^(s,a,w)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Q^(s,a,w) denotes the estimated Q-value for a given state (s) and action (a), parameterized by weights (w).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760292951</data>
    </node>
    <node id="α">
      <data key="d0">α</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
