    <node id="$\int p(y|x,W) \times p(W|X,Y) dW$">
      <data key="d0">$\int p(y|x,W) \times p(W|X,Y) dW$</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">This is an integral expression often used in Bayesian inference, representing a marginal likelihood or predictive distribution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-26c769a26f512a088ad02de1c81c6ddf</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
