      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R_t+2">
      <data key="d0">R_t+2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R_t+2 is the second reward in a sequence, contributing to the sum G_t.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86d0a1a94798eb7b1674502b0ae73cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293089</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R_N">
      <data key="d0">R_N</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">R_N is the final reward in a sequence, contributing to the sum G_t.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86d0a1a94798eb7b1674502b0ae73cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293089</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reward (r(s,a))">
      <data key="d0">Reward (r(s,a))</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term $r(s,a)$ denotes the immediate reward received after taking action $a$ in state $s$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7724d4c011c9981c316498400dd34c58</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value Function (V(s'))">
      <data key="d0">Value Function (V(s'))</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term $V(s')$ represents the value of the next state $s'$, which is the maximum expected future reward achievable from that state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7724d4c011c9981c316498400dd34c58</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Q_t(s, a)">
      <data key="d0">Q_t(s, a)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Q_t(s, a) likely represents an action-value function, which estimates the expected return of taking action 'a' in state 's' at time 't'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Probability 1 - Epsilon">
      <data key="d0">Probability 1 - Epsilon</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Probability 1 - Epsilon is the likelihood with which the action A_t is chosen from the argmax of Q_t(s, a).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Random Action Selection">
      <data key="d0">Random Action Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Random Action Selection is the process where an action 'a' is chosen from a set of possible actions (a_1, ..., a_k) with a probability of epsilon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Action Selection Equation">
      <data key="d0">Action Selection Equation</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Action Selection Equation is a mathematical formula that describes how an action $A_t$ is chosen at a given time $t$.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reinforcement Learning Equation">
      <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning Equation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The equation Q(s, a) = r(s, a) + γV(s') is a fundamental equation in reinforcement learning that defines the action-value function Q.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7724d4c011c9981c316498400dd34c58</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Probability Epsilon">
      <data key="d0">Probability Epsilon</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Probability Epsilon refers to the likelihood of choosing a random action from a set.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Argmax Function">
      <data key="d0">Argmax Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The argmax function returns the argument for which an expression takes its maximum value.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293112</data>
    </node>
    <node id="f(s, a)">
      <data key="d0">f(s, a)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">f(s, a) is a mathematical function that takes state 's' and action 'a' as inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f95cef6c8e603e27b162387295b8935</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1760293131</data>
    </node>
