    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Stochastic Policy">
      <data key="d6">3.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-Learning differs from a stochastic policy by following a greedy policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The stochastic policy contrasts with greedy policies used by Q-Learning agents.&lt;SEP&gt;The stochastic policy contrasts with deterministic policies used in Q-learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">comparison,contrast,policy type</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Agent Models">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The agent's stochastic policy based on A2C contrasts with Q-Learning's greedy policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">contrasts with,methodology</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286219</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Greedy Policy">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-Learning follows a greedy policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Q-Learning operates under a greedy policy, as dictated by the equation.</data>
      <data key="d8">characteristic,employs,follows,uses</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e0300f86edc3c358dfc2a9374e88a8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292339</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Policy Gradient Method">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-learning is compared with Policy Gradient Method.</data>
      <data key="d8">algorithmic differences,comparison</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-4124ebf92b84af2f8bbaecff99882b47</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286324</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Deep Reinforcement Learning">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Deep Reinforcement Learning uses Q-learning as one of its learning algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,technique</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9360ea49ebcfafb62140f053dfc1f70c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286750</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="DeepMind's DQN">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">DeepMind's DQN integrates the algorithm of Q-learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,integration</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286867</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="On-Policy Learning">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">This method of learning, where a single neural network predicts action values, is called on-policy learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Q-Learning is an off-policy method which contrasts with On-Policy Learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">characteristic,comparison,contrast,type</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-08f59209c2113faa8129ee1fd7aa6b8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290143</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Neural Network">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-learning is implemented by stacking actions in one neural network.&lt;SEP&gt;Q-learning's state-action table is replaced by a neural network to handle large-scale tasks.</data>
      <data key="d8">enhancement,implementation,methodology,replacement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de02f58d9cc1d404c5da9c1f45b14fa6</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Experience Replay">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Experience Replay is a key addition to the Q-learning procedure.</data>
      <data key="d8">addition,modification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286998</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Target Network">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A separate target network is used in the Q-learning procedure.</data>
      <data key="d8">addition,modification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286999</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="3x3 SeqTO Environment">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The optimal geometry for the 3x3 SeqTO environment matches the geometry obtained through the tabular Q-Learning algorithm.</data>
      <data key="d8">method validation,result comparison</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e23213a2c2ccb19eb502826a6f80accd</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760287001</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="ε-greedy Approach">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-Learning uses the $\epsilon$-greedy approach to balance exploration and exploitation.</data>
      <data key="d8">strategy,uses</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9fa18d38be749cd12e05de349dfa07cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760287126</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Watkins and Dayan 1992">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q-Learning was developed in 1989, as described in Watkins and Dayan (1992).</data>
      <data key="d8">development,publication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9fa18d38be749cd12e05de349dfa07cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760287127</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning" target="Action Value Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
