    <edge source="Model Architecture" target="Variable Input Sequence Length">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A model architecture is required to handle variable input sequence length.</data>
      <data key="d8">handling,requirement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286345</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Model Architecture" target="1D Sequence">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A model architecture is required to handle variable input sequence length, where torque-speed points are represented as a 1D sequence.</data>
      <data key="d8">data handling,sequence processing</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286353</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Model Architecture" target="RNNs">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">RNNs with an attention mechanism are a popular DL algorithm for sequence-to-sequence modeling, suited for the model architecture.</data>
      <data key="d8">algorithm selection,deep learning</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286353</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Model Architecture" target="Attention Mechanism">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The model architecture incorporates an attention mechanism to mitigate information loss and improve performance for long sequences.</data>
      <data key="d8">mitigation,performance improvement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286354</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Model Architecture" target="Parameter Sharing">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The model architecture handles variable sequence lengths due to the property of parameter sharing in RNNs and time-distributed feedforward networks.</data>
      <data key="d8">adaptability,design principle</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7d489b649275341aa1660eded71c88c4</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286356</data>
    </edge>
