    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="A2C Based Agent">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An A2C based agent derives its action from a stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">characteristic,derives action from</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286228</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Action">
      <data key="d6">3.0</data>
      <data key="d7">In a stochastic policy, multiple actions can be selected with a non-zero probability.&lt;SEP&gt;A stochastic policy defines the probability of an agent taking action 'a'.&lt;SEP&gt;$\\pi_{\\boldsymbol{\\theta}}(a | \\boldsymbol{s})$ represents the probability of taking a specific action $a$.</data>
      <data key="d8">action selection,decision-making,defines probability for,predicts probability for,probability distribution</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7545e109d55e050bca56ba6604cda3ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="State">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A stochastic policy is conditioned on the current state 's'.&lt;SEP&gt;$\\pi_{\\boldsymbol{\\theta}}(a | \\boldsymbol{s})$ represents the probability of taking an action when the agent is in state $\\boldsymbol{s}$.</data>
      <data key="d8">conditioned on,context,is dependent on,models behavior in</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291163</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Multiple Optimal Geometries">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The different nature of deterministic and stochastic policy is the sole reason for multiple optimal geometries.</data>
      <data key="d8">outcome,reason for</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-12274febd6bccf438d9cbc6fce42afe1</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286234</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Probability Distribution">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The randomness in action selection for a stochastic policy depends on the probability distribution over the action space.&lt;SEP&gt;The stochastic policy mathematically represents the probability distribution over possible actions given the current state.</data>
      <data key="d8">defines,governance,mechanism,represents</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7133594b2e19b403575b42aef1cafffb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291162</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Policy Gradient">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Policy Gradient trains a stochastic policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Policy Gradient methods are used to optimize the parameters of a stochastic policy defined by the equation.</data>
      <data key="d8">implementation,optimization,training,utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7133594b2e19b403575b42aef1cafffb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290736</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Exploration &amp; Exploitation">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Exploration is influenced by the probability distribution of actions trained by a stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">balancing,strategy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-7133594b2e19b403575b42aef1cafffb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760287073</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Action Probability">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation describes how the probability of selecting a particular action is determined by a stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">definition,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290734</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Softmax Function">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation represents a softmax function applied to action preferences to define a stochastic policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The stochastic policy is defined by a softmax function.</data>
      <data key="d8">implementation,mathematical representation,mechanism</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290735</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Function Approximator">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The stochastic policy's output is based on a function approximator's output.</data>
      <data key="d8">implementation,output</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290736</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Actor-Critic">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">In Actor-Critic methods, the 'Actor' component learns this stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">policy representation,utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290737</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="theta">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The variable 'theta' parameterizes the stochastic policy function.</data>
      <data key="d8">control,parameterization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290738</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="f(s, a, theta)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The output of 'f(s, a, theta)' contributes to the calculation of the stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,input</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290738</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Exploration">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The stochastic nature of the policy is central to enabling exploration in Reinforcement Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;The probabilistic nature of a stochastic policy is crucial for exploration in Reinforcement Learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">characteristic,enables,facilitates,mechanism</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9012606caf5dec3e73821be7188dc6cf</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290739</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Differentiability">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The stochastic policy's differentiability with respect to its parameters is crucial for gradient-based optimization.</data>
      <data key="d8">optimization,requirement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290739</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Actor">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Actor in Actor-Critic determines the stochastic policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">output,role</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290740</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="Exploration vs. Exploitation">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The stochastic policy directly addresses the exploration vs. exploitation dilemma.&lt;SEP&gt;The stochastic nature of the policy addresses the exploration-exploitation dilemma by assigning probabilities to actions.</data>
      <data key="d8">balance,balancing,mechanism</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290741</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stochastic Policy" target="PPO Algorithms">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Softmax policies are widely used in PPO algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,usage</data>
