      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Okamoto observed that optimized results of density-based methods depend on initial conditions.</data>
      <data key="d8">observation,research</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286401</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="TO">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Density-based methods are a type of TO method.</data>
      <data key="d8">category,method</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286405</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Fixed Domain Of Finite Elements">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Density-based methods operate within a fixed domain of finite elements to optimize an objective function.</data>
      <data key="d8">operation,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Objective Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Density-based methods optimize the objective function by determining whether each element should be solid material or void.</data>
      <data key="d8">determination,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286412</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Interpolation Functions">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Density-based methods adopt interpolation functions where material properties are interpreted as continuous design variables.</data>
      <data key="d8">adoption,interpretation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286412</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Discrete Variables">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">In density-based methods, discrete variables are transferred to continuous variables.</data>
      <data key="d8">continuity,transformation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286413</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Continuous Variables">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An optimizer uses continuous variables to iteratively steer the solution in density-based methods.</data>
      <data key="d8">iterative process,utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286413</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Penalty Methods">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Penalty methods are utilized in density-based methods to force the solution to crisp "0/1" or "solid/void" topologies.</data>
      <data key="d8">enforcement,utilization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286414</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Regularization">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Regularization is adopted in density-based methods to alleviate the checkerboard problem and mesh-dependency issue.</data>
      <data key="d8">adoption,alleviation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-31b45185f3e33b63259454671f7614ad</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760286415</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Density-Based Methods" target="Filter Techniques">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Filter techniques are adopted in density-based methods to alleviate the checkerboard problem and mesh-dependency issue.</data>
