      <data key="d6">3.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The rotor tries to move to a position of least reluctance with respect to the stator.&lt;SEP&gt;Excitation in the stator poles controls the movement of the rotor.&lt;SEP&gt;The rotor is an internal component located within the stator of the electric motor.</data>
