    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="Equation: Q(s, a) = r(s, a) + γV(s')">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation mathematically defines the Q-value function.</data>
      <data key="d8">definition,describes</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289702</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="Value Of The Successor State">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Q-value function's definition incorporates the discounted value of the successor state $V(s')$.</data>
      <data key="d8">components,definition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289709</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="Bellman Expectation Equation">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Q-value function equation is a form of the Bellman expectation equation, formalizing the total value of taking an action.</data>
      <data key="d8">formalization,theoretical basis</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289710</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="Advantage Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Q-value function is directly used in simplifying the calculation of the Advantage function, where $A(s, a) = Q(s, a) - V(s)$.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,derivation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289711</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="State-Value Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Q-value function explicitly depends on the state-value function $V(s')$ of the next state.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependency,relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289712</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Value Function" target="SARSA">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">SARSA is a practical application of the Q-value function for on-policy learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,methodology</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-827b20ce2e241ba2e3eb418463078226</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289713</data>
    </edge>
