      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289870</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return Gt" target="Reward Rt+1">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return Gt is defined as the sum of the immediate Reward Rt+1 and the future Return Gt+1.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,definition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87755691ed2aadfe9652dad2d067f4a9</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291597</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return Gt" target="Return Gt+1">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return Gt is defined recursively as including the Return Gt+1.</data>
      <data key="d8">definition,recursive relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-87755691ed2aadfe9652dad2d067f4a9</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291598</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient-Based Optimization" target="Parameters Theta">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The parameters theta are updated using gradient-based optimization methods.</data>
      <data key="d8">learning,modification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient-Based Optimization" target="Differentiability">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Differentiability allows for the application of gradient-based optimization methods.</data>
      <data key="d8">enabling factor,prerequisite</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b470eacdde6ba3189132ab26e9634120</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760290745</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neural Network Policy" target="Policy Parameters ($\theta_t$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The policy parameters $\theta$ represent the weights of a neural network policy.</data>
      <data key="d8">composition,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289887</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Policy Parameters ($\theta_{t+1}$)" target="Policy Parameters ($\theta_t$)">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The new parameters $\theta_{t+1}$ are obtained by adding a vector to $\theta_t$.&lt;SEP&gt;$\theta_{t+1}$ is updated from $\theta_t$ in the equation.</data>
      <data key="d8">iteration,update mechanism,update rule,vector addition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289884</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Policy Parameters ($\theta_t$)" target="Gradient of Performance Measure ($\nabla J (\theta_t)$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The gradient of the performance measure is evaluated with respect to the current policy parameters $\theta_t$.</data>
      <data key="d8">gradient evaluation,parameter dependence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289885</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Policy Parameters ($\theta_t$)" target="Performance Measure ($J$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The agent aims to maximize $J$ by adjusting its policy parameters.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependence,maximization target</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289886</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Performance Measure ($J$)" target="Gradient Operator ($\nabla$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The gradient operator computes partial derivatives of the performance measure $J$.</data>
      <data key="d8">operation,target</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289887</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Performance Measure ($J$)" target="Probability of Action Selection ($p(a)$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The performance measure $J$ depends on the probability of action selection $p(a)$.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependence,influence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289888</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Performance Measure ($J$)" target="Return ($G_t$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Return ($G_t$) is used to estimate the gradient of $J$.</data>
      <data key="d8">estimation,measure</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6a27902bb1d11b0f453eb766cb38c22a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760289889</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scalar Multiplication" target="Gradient Vector">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Scalar multiplication scales the gradient vector by the learning rate.</data>
      <data key="d8">modification,scaling</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c35bf46c88c50e423b73a91a41f7f95a</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291859</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Immediate Reward ($R_k$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return ($G_t$) is defined as a finite sum of Immediate Rewards ($R_k$) received over a specific time horizon.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,summation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291004</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Time Step ($t$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return ($G_t$) represents the expected accumulation of rewards starting from Time Step ($t$).</data>
      <data key="d8">calculated from,temporal context</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291005</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Final Time Step ($N$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The summation for Return ($G_t$) terminates at the Final Time Step ($N$), indicating the end of an episode.</data>
      <data key="d8">episode end,summation limit</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291006</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Value Functions ($Q(s,a)$ or $V(s)$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The concept of Return ($G_t$) lays the groundwork for Value Functions ($Q(s,a)$ or $V(s)$).</data>
      <data key="d8">derived concept,foundation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291006</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Discount Factor ($\gamma$)">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Discount Factor ($\gamma$) modifies the basic definition of Return ($G_t$) to create a 'discounted return'.&lt;SEP&gt;The return ($G_t$) involves a summation of future rewards possibly discounted by the discount factor.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation dependency,component,influence,modification</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19e84f4051b2d1d639403e518dc4ebb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291430</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Summation">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return ($G_t$) typically involves a summation of future rewards.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation method,involves</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a19e84f4051b2d1d639403e518dc4ebb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291436</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Reward ($R_{t+k}$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return ($G_t$) is composed of the sum of future Rewards ($R_{t+k}$) received at subsequent time steps.</data>
      <data key="d8">composition,summation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291492</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Monte Carlo (MC) Methods">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Monte Carlo (MC) Methods directly use the empirical (true) observed Return ($G_t$) from completed episodes to update value functions.</data>
      <data key="d8">methodology,usage</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291494</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="Off-Line Policy Evaluation">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The calculation of Return ($G_t$) is used in Off-Line Policy Evaluation to quantify the utility of states or state-action pairs.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,utility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291496</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Return ($G_t$)" target="True Return">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Return ($G_t$) represents the `True Return` or `absolute return` for a given episode.</data>
      <data key="d8">representation,synonym</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-34ed3729fa06a3c6f2093a4d16a2c572</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291497</data>
    </edge>
