    <edge source="Return in Markov Decision Process and Reinforcement Learning" target="$$ G _ { t } \doteq R _ { t + 1 } + R _ { t + 2 } + . . . + R _ { N } $$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation $$ G _ { t } \doteq R _ { t + 1 } + R _ { t + 2 } + . . . + R _ { N } $$ defines the concept of 'Return' in the context of a Markov Decision Process (MDP) and Reinforcement Learning (RL).</data>
      <data key="d8">definition,representation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291007</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$$ G _ { t } \doteq R _ { t + 1 } + R _ { t + 2 } + . . . + R _ { N } $$" target="Finite-Horizon Episodic Task">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The summation terminating at N in the equation implies a finite-horizon episodic task where the sequence of actions and rewards has a clear end point.</data>
      <data key="d8">context,implication</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291008</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="R_k" target="Magnetic Field Distribution Values in C-Core Armature">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">R_k, the immediate reward, could be the 'magnetic field distribution values in the C-core armature' in the context of a C-core design problem.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,example</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-d9b95c8542f91fd870d1bfec5dbdecfb</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291008</data>
    </edge>
