    </edge>
    <edge source="J" target="$\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}} J$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}} J$ is the gradient of the performance measure J, used for optimizing the performance measure.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292223</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="J" target="Nabla J">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nabla J is the gradient of the performance measure J with respect to the policy parameters.</data>
      <data key="d8">gradient,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292228</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="J" target="G t">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">J is defined as a measure of all rewards similar to the return G t.</data>
      <data key="d8">definition,similarity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292230</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}} J$" target="$\nabla l o g ( \pi ( a _ { t } | s _ { t } ; \boldsymbol { \theta } ) )$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}} J$ is proportional to the gradient of the logarithm of the policy's probability.</data>
      <data key="d8">mathematical operation,proportional to</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292225</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theta" target="Nabla J">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nabla J indicates the rate of change of J with respect to Theta.</data>
      <data key="d8">gradient,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292230</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theta" target="Nabla Log Policy">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nabla Log Policy is the gradient with respect to the parameters Theta.</data>
      <data key="d8">gradient,parameter</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292234</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theta" target="Pi">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Theta leads to Pi, indicating a further transformation from Theta to an output represented by Pi.</data>
      <data key="d8">output,transformation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0b9ed49570cc7fd3b04f001bb2371e8b</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292969</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="G t" target="J($\boldsymbol{\theta}$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">J($\boldsymbol{\theta}$) is similar to the return G t.</data>
      <data key="d8">evaluation,relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292236</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nabla Log Policy" target="Score Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nabla Log Policy is often called the 'score function'.</data>
      <data key="d8">alias,definition</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-890e76382b57a11ba9855a8134986055</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292235</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule" target="TD Target">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The TD Target is the target value used in the Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule for updating the Q-value.</data>
      <data key="d8">basis for update,reference value</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292263</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule" target="Temporal-Difference Learning">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation is explicitly described as a temporal-difference (TD) learning update, a core component of Q-learning.</data>
      <data key="d8">methodology,update_rule</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292265</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule" target="Learning Rate ($ \alpha $)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The learning rate ($\alpha$) directly scales the TD error within the Q-learning update rule, controlling the step size of the update.</data>
      <data key="d8">parameter_influence,scaling</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292266</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule" target="Reward ($ R_{t+1} $)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The immediate reward ($R_{t+1}$) is a key component contributing to the TD target in the Q-learning update rule.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,input</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292267</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Q-Learning Temporal-Difference Update Rule" target="Discount Factor ($ \gamma $)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The discount factor ($\gamma$) is applied to future rewards within the TD target of the Q-learning update rule.</data>
      <data key="d8">component,parameter_influence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292268</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Reward (R_{t+1})" target="TD Target">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Reward (R_{t+1}) is a component of the TD Target.</data>
      <data key="d8">component of,contributes to</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292260</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="State (s_{t+1})" target="TD Target">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">s_{t+1} is used to calculate the maximum Q-value for the TD Target.</data>
      <data key="d8">component of,context for</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-258e29a004ed4a9ecd38f72b2c0d91d8</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$A_t$" target="Current State $s$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$A_t$ is selected by the agent based on the current state $s$.</data>
      <data key="d8">context,dependency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292302</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$A_t$" target="Action $a$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$A_t$ is the selected action, which can be either the greedy action or a random action $a$.</data>
      <data key="d8">outcome,selection</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292305</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Exploration Parameter ($\epsilon$)" target="Probability of Greedy Action ($1-\epsilon$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The exploration parameter $\epsilon$ determines the probability of selecting the greedy action.</data>
      <data key="d8">determines</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292298</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Exploration Parameter ($\epsilon$)" target="Probability of Random Action ($\epsilon$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The exploration parameter $\epsilon$ determines the probability of selecting a random action.</data>
      <data key="d8">determines</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292299</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Topology Optimization Results" target="Electromagnetic Actuators">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Topology optimization results are relevant to electromagnetic actuators, such as the C-core example.</data>
      <data key="d8">application domain,context</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292304</data>
    </edge>
