    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="Deep Q-Network Algorithms">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The underlying principle of Error (MSE) is used in training neural networks for Deep Q-Network Algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,principle</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f74efd7c2930be98c8e7ee58bb7f2201</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292619</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="R_t">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Error (MSE) depends on R_t as part of its calculation.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-feffff69e0f56312f2846d9f57d0a4f7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292893</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="max_{a'} Q(S_{t+1}, A_{t+1}, w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Error (MSE) incorporates max_{a'} Q(S_{t+1}, A_{t+1}, w) in its calculation.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-feffff69e0f56312f2846d9f57d0a4f7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292894</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="Q(S_t, A_t, w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Error (MSE) uses Q(S_t, A_t, w) in its calculation.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-feffff69e0f56312f2846d9f57d0a4f7</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292895</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="Q (s, a, w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Error (MSE) is calculated using Q (s, a, w) as a component.</data>
      <data key="d8">calculation,component</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292957</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="Q*(s,a)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Error (MSE) is calculated using the difference involving Q*(s,a).</data>
      <data key="d8">comparison,measurement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292958</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Error (MSE)" target="Q^(s,a,w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Error (MSE) is calculated using the difference involving Q^(s,a,w).</data>
      <data key="d8">comparison,measurement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-85055739dbffbeba952630d321118334</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292959</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="State-Value Function Approximation" target="Electromagnetic Device Design">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation for State-Value Function Approximation is central to optimizing Electromagnetic Device Design.</data>
      <data key="d8">application domain</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292645</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="State-Value Function Approximation" target="Section 5.3">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation for State-Value Function Approximation is a cornerstone of Section 5.3.</data>
      <data key="d8">cornerstone,focus</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292649</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Equation: $\\hat { v } ( s , w ) \\approx v _ { \\pi } ( s )$" target="Electromagnetic Device Design Optimization">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The equation is central to the setup of Deep Reinforcement Learning for optimizing electromagnetic device design.</data>
      <data key="d8">application,context</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292640</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Value Function ($\\hat { v } ( s , w )$)" target="True State-Value Function ($v _ { \\pi } ( s )$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Estimated Value Function approximates the True State-Value Function.</data>
      <data key="d8">approximation,estimation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292639</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Value Function ($\\hat { v } ( s , w )$)" target="Action Value Function Predictor ($\\hat { Q } ( s , a , w )$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Estimated Value Function (state-value) is related to the Action Value Function Predictor ($Q$-value).</data>
      <data key="d8">related concept,relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292641</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Value Function ($\\hat { v } ( s , w )$)" target="State-value Function ($\\hat { V } ( s , w )$)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Estimated Value Function $\\hat { v } ( s , w )$ is a specific form of a State-value Function $\\hat { V } ( s , w )$.</data>
      <data key="d8">representation,synonymy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292642</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Value Function" target="True State-Value Function">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Estimated Value Function ($\hat { v } ( s , w )$) serves as an approximation ($\approx$) of the True State-Value Function ($v _ { \\pi } ( s )$).</data>
      <data key="d8">approximation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6aa75c1dcbd4f8e8da642ba3e55f2a1c</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292645</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="(Lei et al. 2019)" target="k-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), Support Vector Machine (SVM)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(Lei et al. 2019) utilize k-Nearest Neighbors and Support Vector Machine as their learning architecture.</data>
      <data key="d8">learning architecture,uses</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b3676b77d4e3057ccce502057364cbae</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291044</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="(Yu et al. 2019)" target="Convolutional Neural Network (CNN), Conditional Generative Adversarial Network (cGAN)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(Yu et al. 2019) utilize a hybrid of Convolutional Neural Network and Conditional Generative Adversarial Network as their learning architecture.</data>
      <data key="d8">learning architecture,uses</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-b3676b77d4e3057ccce502057364cbae</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760291046</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$Q_t(s, a)$" target="Current State $s$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$Q_t(s, a)$ is the action-value function for a given current state $s$.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependency,relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292304</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$Q_t(s, a)$" target="Action $a$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">$Q_t(s, a)$ is the action-value function for a given action $a$.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependency,relationship</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292306</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="$Q_t(s, a)$" target="$\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The $\\arg\\max_{a} Q_t(s, a)$ operator calculates the action $a$ that maximizes the Q-value for $Q_t(s, a)$.</data>
      <data key="d8">dependency,maximization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-dbd39005d698bcd623fe368243dbe14d</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292307</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Maximum Future Action-Value" target="max Q(S_t+1, A_t+1, w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">max Q(S_t+1, A_t+1, w) represents the estimated maximum future action-value from the next state.</data>
      <data key="d8">representation,variable</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a24ed737fb6aa8500ccd706bf246c499</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292509</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Estimated Action-Value" target="Q(S_t, A_t, w)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Q(S_t, A_t, w) represents the estimated action-value for the current state and action.</data>
      <data key="d8">representation,variable</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a24ed737fb6aa8500ccd706bf246c499</data>
      <data key="d10">Khan_Arbaaz_ECE_Thesis.pdf</data>
      <data key="d11">1760292510</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="A_t" target="Q_t(s, a)">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A_t is determined by an optimization process involving Q_t(s, a) under certain probabilities.</data>
      <data key="d8">action selection,optimization</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760293116</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="A_t" target="Probability 1 - Epsilon">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">With probability 1 - Epsilon, A_t is chosen as the action that maximizes Q_t(s, a).</data>
      <data key="d8">choice mechanism,likelihood</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0604f5005a60d070243b26410ba10b20</data>
      <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d11">1760293118</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="A_t" target="Random Action Selection">
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">With probability epsilon, A_t is chosen randomly from the set (a_1, ..., a_k).</data>
      <data key="d8">alternative choice,likelihood</data>
